t to shame someone about how serious it is, perhaps you are not on as firm a ground as you may think, argument wise.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It has occurred to me that the various WoD games would have really benefited from having something similar to Scion's setting dials in each of their respective Storyteller Handbooks, with advice on tuning the game to your group's preferences. Do you want Mage to feel more like Hellblazer or The Matrix? Vampire more or less broody? Werewolf more or less satirical? How much secret elder vampire cult conspiracy? How much violence? Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T11:15:40-07:00","id":1539150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539117#post1539117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my Malkavian character. &quot;Dressing up like something from the Underworld movies is a surefire way to draw the wrong kind of attention and it's usually laughter.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because I became immortal to dress in flannel. - Toreador","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T15:16:21-07:00","id":1539170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539150#post1539150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, because I became immortal to dress in flannel. - Toreador</div> </div> </div> </div>Be like the old WW writing guide's admonitions to always write in active voice, wear bondage gear with your flannel!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T15:51:06-07:00","id":1539260,"title":"","content":"How did we wind up dressing up as something out of a Clive Barker story?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T15:03:09-07:00","id":1539343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539019#post1539019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the TLDR version of my response is.<br /> <br /> &quot;This is a game about playing a magical zombie in the Modern Day that has fooled everyone and have their own mafia. If you want to shame someone about how serious it is, perhaps you are not on as firm a ground as you may think, argument wise.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're gonna get mad at me for saying this, but I personally think that the strict metaplot zealotry and this insistence on forcing a specific view of &quot;Street Level True Art Personal Horror&quot; on the part of the devs that began during Revised, continued into Requiem and cooled off a bit when V20 was metaplot-agnostic is kinda what led to all this.<br /> <br /> Too many devs got concerned people were &quot;playing the game wrong&quot; and used the metaplot to try and police the setting of anything that was remotely seen as &quot;cool&quot; or &quot;gonzo&quot; (or just something that a specific dev happened to not like) to try and force a very specific view of personal horror. All of the pretentious hand-wringing over trenchcoats and katanas or Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand is what ultimately led to where we are now with the IP.<br /> <br /> And yes, while Revised had plenty of gonzo moments, they were all done in service of the metaplot and back then, the devs were notorious for shaming and chiding readers about badwrongfun in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539136#post1539136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has occurred to me that the various WoD games would have really benefited from having something similar to Scion's setting dials in each of their respective Storyteller Handbooks, with advice on tuning the game to your group's preferences. Do you want Mage to feel more like Hellblazer or The Matrix? Vampire more or less broody? Werewolf more or less satirical? How much secret elder vampire cult conspiracy? How much violence? Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would've been amazing.<br /> <br /> But for some reason, Revised-era White Wolf devs had this weird fixation on badwrongfun and the V5 in all of its various incarnations feel like it took all the wrong lessons from that era<br /> <br /> Scion was White Wolf too but there was something about the WoD IP specifically that must've gotten them worked up about people &quot;playing the game wrong&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 07-26-2024, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T13:04:55-07:00","id":1539493,"title":"","content":"How do you play the game wrong? Our group just use the metaplot as an outline but nothing set in stone as it gives us creative options to play around with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T17:44:24-07:00","id":1539510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539493#post1539493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you play the game wrong? Our group just use the metaplot as an outline but nothing set in stone as it gives us creative options to play around with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know either but a very vocal toxic subgroup of the WoD fanbase seem to think if you're not playing street-level no-combat/low-combat &quot;True Art Personal Horror&quot; pretentious angstfests that adhere strictly to the metaplot, you're somehow playing the game wrong. The constant handwringing about &quot;Muh Supers With Fangs! Muh Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas!&quot; has been going on since at least Revised Edition.<br /> <br /> A major factor behind the decisions with V5's metaplot, setting, and gameplay changes were that they were put in place to actively take away options or elements of the setting from players, so that &quot;the wrong kind&quot; of players would be dis-incentivized to play, and this is a recurring element of V5 from the original Martin Ericsson-led Parawolf to Modiphius to Renegade Studios.<br /> <br /> And yes, it's exactly as asinine as it sounds.<br /> <br /> While I personally don't care for angsty highbrow &quot;personal horror&quot; or following the metaplot, I'm not going to say it doesn't have a place at the gaming table and if I were in charge of the gameline, I wouldn't impose radical mechanical and setting changes to try and force players to &quot;play the game right&quot; either<br /> <br /> The metaplot-agnostic approach of V20 was best because it more or less said &quot;This is a celebration of Vampire in its entirety. All editions, all gameplay styles, and all variants of the setting. Whatever your preference is, it's all good.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T12:57:10-07:00","id":1539551,"title":"","content":"That can certainly ruin a good game Matt. We do more of a James Bond/Sherlock Holmes and Sons Of Anarchy type of vibe in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T23:06:40-07:00","id":1539576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539343#post1539343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But for some reason, Revised-era White Wolf devs had this weird fixation on badwrongfun and the V5 in all of its various incarnations feel like it took all the wrong lessons from that era</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of that was mostly Justin Achilli (and to a lesser extent Rob Hatch). Ethan Skemp really did not care one way or the other. (The minor exception, IIRC, was that he found people trying to play werewolves as furries to be off-putting.) Jess Heinig was honestly too busy dealing with dictates from upper management (which included Mage's shifts in tone and focus, something Jess had zero control over) and certain friends/fans of Phil Brocato who made him the scapegoat for upper management's decision to have Phil step down as Mage developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T07:36:51-07:00","id":1539588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool#post1538996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://beforewegoblog.com/review-vampire-the-masquerade-walk-among-us-by-various/\" target=\"_blank\">https://beforewegoblog.com/review-va...us-by-various/</a><br /> <br /> VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE: WALK AMONG US is the first and possibly last World of Darkness novel we\u2019re likely to see since the end of the Old World of Darkness in 2004. The premise for Vampire: The Masquerade is that the world is secretly ruled from the shadows by a variety of supernatural beings (chiefly vampires) and they are constantly feuding for power like mafia bosses. It was an immensely fun premise if you were a counterculture Goth kid or just a guy who enjoyed playing edgy antiheroes, both of which described me. In 2018, the Old World of Darkness was revived with Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition and the results have been controversial ever since.<br /> <br /> Walk Among Us, in it\u2019s own way, is the perfect encapsulation of why the design philosophy of 5th Edition has been hit or miss. The book is three novellas by Genevieve Gornichec, Caitlin Starling, and Cassandra Khaw (the latter of mine is a personal favorite). The authors are each incredibly talented, create a believable World of Darkness, and write stories that are excellent pieces of horror each. This out of the way, no shade upon their writing abilities, I kind of hate this book. Walk Among Us is something that represents pretty much everything I don\u2019t want out of the New-New World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> The Old World of Darkness was, in simple, a comic book. Specifically, it was a very Nineties comic book. You were a dark and brooding antihero who sat on rooftops next to gargoyles and surveyed the corrupt city full of rival supernaturals as you pondered your lost humanity. There\u2019s a reason that Underworld is a guilty pleasure and Blade is probably closer to Vampire: The Masquerade than it ever was the character from Tomb of Dracula. Yes, you feasted upon blood, but the power fantasy was also present as was the romance.<br /> <br /> Walk Among Us reflects the 5th Edition mindset that being a vampire is not just awful. You aren\u2019t just tormented with generic angst and tragic backstory. No, worse, being a vampire is not cool. The protagonists of these three stories are some of the whiniest most unlikable vampires in fiction. So much so that Louis of Interview with a Vampire would say they\u2019re a bunch of losers. This is perhaps the ultimate in unforgivable sins and why I cannot endorse these three disgraces to Caine.<br /> <br /> It\u2019d be alright if these vampires whined because they didn\u2019t want to be murderers, they lost their families, or even mourned the loss of the Sun in some tragic Gothic way. No, they\u2019re all scumbags with no morality to offend against. It\u2019s the fact that being a vampire doesn\u2019t make them any less annoying than the kind of jerks they were in life.<br /> <br /> \u201cA Sheep Among Wolves\u201d protagonist, Clea, starts sympathetically enough but her primary concern once she\u2019s joined a radical student activist group is to make sure the leader continues to like her even when she\u2019s committing arson/murder for no apparent reward. She doesn\u2019t even have any politics, she just feels really lonely on campus. Being a vampire just is another label to her and not one that invokes any curiosity. My wife shares some of Clea\u2019s issues but found her equally frustrating.<br /> <br /> \u201cFine Print\u201d follows the world\u2019s dumbest Ventrue. Duke negotiates a contract with his sire before his Embrace, apparently assuming this is legally enforceable, and is obnoxious the entire way through. He also doesn\u2019t bother to learn that he can\u2019t eat food beforehand, that sunlight forces him to sleep, or that vampires like him need special kinds of blood to drink. This probably my favorite of the stories and Duke really should have been staked for the Sun on his first night.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Land of Milk and Honey\u201d follows a vegan Toreador Anarch who runs a commune of blood harvesters that raise their own food as well as animals. Leigh is among the absolute worst kind of lifestyle advocates who basically keeps her subordinates as animals to harvest but insists on it being the more humane alternative. Its blackly funny that other Kindred seem to think of her as an extreme pro-vegan type in-universe but listening to her ramble on about her ideology the entire time just makes me want to see the Sabbat arrive.<br /> <br /> This is the heart of perhaps 5th Edition\u2019s biggest flaw as there\u2019s nothing particularly fun about being a vampire. Walk Among Us\u2018 vampires are not sexy, cool, or particularly powerful. They have no torment from the fact they\u2019re good people forced to be evil by hunger or circumstance. Christof may have been a somewhat cliche example of a reluctant vampire, but he was interesting as a Crusader turned monster. Lucita may be evil, but she had tragedy, pathos, and sex appeal. These guys are like the obnoxious lady at the supermarket being turned into Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the review.<br /> <br /> V5 never got me, I enjoyed Winter's Teeth comic book though. Perhaps someday I'll read this novel but highly unlikely.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T09:33:08-07:00","id":1539592,"title":"","content":"While I liked V5 enough when I oplwned it honestly it just wasn't enough for me to keep the books. This basically boiled down to the fact that at the end of the day any group is playing for fun. It's why my personal favourite WoD game is Werewolf, it easily slides from serious business to 'rip and tear' without feeling like someone's yelling 'wrongbadfun'. Although I've heard W5 changes that.<br /> <br /> But at the end of the day it doesn't matter how serious you set up your urban fantasy/horror game to be, three quarters of characters will show up in a trenchcoat. Because a player's primary goal is to have fun, and to a lot fangpions and vampire slugfests are more entertaining than miralising.<br /> <br /> And if things get too gonzo? I think people underestimate how scary the ridiculous can be. Whether that's Nazi penguins coming out of Antarctica or that one crazy mage who desperately wants every last Yu-Gi-Oh card, you can make it utterly terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T14:03:29-07:00","id":1539603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539576#post1539576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of that was mostly Justin Achilli (and to a lesser extent Rob Hatch). Ethan Skemp really did not care one way or the other. (The minor exception, IIRC, was that he found people trying to play werewolves as furries to be off-putting.) Jess Heinig was honestly too busy dealing with dictates from upper management (which included Mage's shifts in tone and focus, something Jess had zero control over) and certain friends/fans of Phil Brocato who made him the scapegoat for upper management's decision to have Phil step down as Mage developer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come to think of it, Justin Achilli does seem to be the common denominator in all of the edition warring, ideological purity spirals, and the general state of WoD as both an IP and a fandom from 1999 onward....<br /> <br /> He spearheaded the majority of Revised's run, oversaw the development of the Requiem 1e corebook (I'm pretty sure the whole &quot;No emotions&quot; fluff was his doing specifically), and while he did oversee V20, that was a group effort where they brought in as many people from the old days as they could, and he's also been heavily involved in Parawolf/V5 in both official and unofficial capacities from the looks of it.<br /> <br /> Martin Ericsson and his <i>de facto</i> successor Karim Muammar both seem to be ideological disciples of Justin Achilli too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 07-31-2024, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T02:57:58-07:00","id":1539628,"title":"","content":"I will note that Vampire has always had this weird mix of influences.<br /> On the one hand, it is an early 90s &quot;street level&quot; urban fantasy RPG, and so is built with a lot of the same assumptions as things like Cyberpunk 2020, Kult, Nightlife, and TMNT &amp; Other Strangeness. This being that the PCs are essentially the protagonists of some sort of Hard-Boiled Detective or Film Noir story, individuals with some useful skills who exist on the edges of normal society, tend to get sucked in to dangerous situations, and (usually) have at least some sort of degree of morality that puts them above the predators they encounter in either the gutters, the working world, or high society. Sure, you may be an outcast, a jerk, or even a freak in the eyes of normal society, but you are (probably) better than the amoral sociopaths you find yourself confronting.<br /> On the other hand, it is a setting that is almost entirely based off of a trilogy of vampire novels which start with a fairly grounded account of one man's experience of being a vampire and ends with a 4000-year-old blood god trying to take over the world. So certain aspects of the setting clash with certain aspects of the RPG design, running the risk of PCs being reduced to helpless bystanders or having to engage in some sort of arms race to create PCs who can actually compete with the blood gods. In addition, that particular style of vampire fiction and its fandom tended to lend itself to very social-oriented settings, scenes, and play styles (especially LARPing). And that can clash with some of the more &quot;traditional&quot; focus of some players, the &quot;find the monster, hit the monster&quot; formula.<br /> I don't think there is really a wrong way to play Vampire, although my own preference is essentially Film Noir with certain moral and psychological overtones (probably because I saw the film Angel Heart at such an impressionable age), sometimes veering into more horror or conspiracy areas.<br /> (In hindsight, I really do wish Vampire and the other games had done more books devoted to specific genres and how to do them for your game. Like, this is the Horror genre, its tropes, and how to incorporate them into Vampire. And this is the Political Conspiracy/Mystery genre, this is Gothic Romance, etc. I think the closest we got was Wraith's Love Beyond Death and Mage's Dark Adventure.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T11:29:46-07:00","id":1539648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539628#post1539628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note that Vampire has always had this weird mix of influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with a lot you say. Even in 1e, the game is all over the place. It's explicitly about some kind of personal horror, but a lot of the supplements concentrate on the War of Ages between neonates (frequently Anarchs) and elders (frequently the leaders of the local Camarilla). The Players Guides and ST Handbooks not only have stats for certain types of firearms, but give different stats to different individual weapons within those firearm categories. So we have a half dozen examples of revolvers, another half dozen of light pistols, a half dozen heavy pistols, a half dozen rifles, etc. all with unique stats for damage, difficulty, rate, clip amount, range, etc. We're given stats for grenades, military grade machine guns, artillery systems, antitank weapons, armored fighting vehicles, attack helicopters, and even an F-14 Tomcat. Yeah, those are the type of things I expect in a game of &quot;personal horror&quot;.<br /> <br /> And of course, a lot of that stuff <i>did</i> get used in the games I played in because my play group was mostly a bunch of guys in their late teens who were used to D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> And to be honest, while they were mostly used in ridiculous ways, there will be good players who ask why they can't pull off a scene like they had in Godfather Part III (which just seems to be an ordinary helicopter with multiple guys with submachine guns).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Td8eEM9KDig\" data-code=\"Td8eEM9KDig\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Td8eEM9KDig/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Lots of violence. Of course, some of that was simply us trying to figure out how different roleplaying games would need different play styles. As we played other games than D&amp;D like Vampire and Call of Cthulhu, our playing styles slowly shifted as we realized we could have fun outside of combat. If you ever look at some of the earliest Call of Cthulhu published scenarios, even the original creators had that problem as well. It took a while for them to figure out a better way to approach their game adventures.<br /> <br /> As Vampire attracted new kinds of players and they joined our game group, they were often the ones who first approached the game from different angle because their exposure was not from D&amp;D but because they liked Anne Rice or vampire movies in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539628#post1539628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there is really a wrong way to play Vampire, although my own preference is essentially Film Noir with certain moral and psychological overtones (probably because I saw the film Angel Heart at such an impressionable age), sometimes veering into more horror or conspiracy areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of play styles I don't like, but even though I think certain players are &quot;doing it wrong&quot; and being annoying, I never felt like they should be told they can't be playing that way. I just didn't play with those kind of roleplayers and found other players whose style were more in tune with my own. It's about having fun, not trying to meet someone's arbitrary definition of what is allowed.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I might insult some players behind their back for their playing style, but I'd never do it to their face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_I7f4ALqojg\" data-code=\"_I7f4ALqojg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_I7f4ALqojg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539628#post1539628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(In hindsight, I really do wish Vampire and the other games had done more books devoted to specific genres and how to do them for your game. Like, this is the Horror genre, its tropes, and how to incorporate them into Vampire. And this is the Political Conspiracy/Mystery genre, this is Gothic Romance, etc. I think the closest we got was Wraith's Love Beyond Death and Mage's Dark Adventure.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This would have been a great thing, and it was something I always hoped the Storyteller Guides would address - giving us toolkits and options so STs can customize their games. I can understand why the earliest editions didn't, but it was a big disappointment when the Revised versions did not.<br /> <br /> In the late eighties and early nineties, we had lots of different kinds of vampire movies. Coppola's Dracula, Lost Boys, Innocent Blood, Near Dark, Fright Night, Interview with the Vampire, and many others all had very different takes on the vampire story. And VtM did support most of that in terms of having available concepts that could be utilized. But that's different than explicit guidance on emulating different kind of genres which new and inexperienced GMs often need.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T12:25:08-07:00","id":1539655,"title":"","content":"I think part of the reason that many games did either take on the form of Noir Style Mysteries, \u2018Superhero\u2019 Beat-em-Ups, or even Political Thrillers is that, \u2018personal horror\u2019 as a stand-alone concept, is kind of tricky to conceive of in a game-able fashion. I\u2019m a fairly regular reader of the Alexandrian blog and his posts and game structure is something that I\u2019ve thought about a lot re: Vampire (and other WoD games).<br /> <br /> I think one of the things that makes Mysteries, Action, &amp; Politics so attractive for vampire is that they each provide a tentpole structure which is useful both to player and ST. If the game is about Mysteries then the PCs need to investigate and the ST needs to write mystery plots for their game. If it\u2019s about Action then the PCs need to fight and the ST needs to prepare conflicts for their game. If the game is about Politics then the PCs need to conspire and the ST needs to prepare intrigues for their game. Those are all easier to grok then Freeform \u2018personal horror\u2019 and one can even weave personal horror into each of these pillars. But if one doesn\u2019t have a pillar and is just going for personal horror, what does that look like in play?<br /> <br /> Interview with the Vampire can keep us invested in Louis and Lestat\u2019s inner turmoil, whether in the form of novel or film or show, far more easily then we can construct frames for such narratives at our tables, at least in my experience (although LARP and play-by-post has such advantages in this regard, imo). <br /> <br /> These things aren\u2019t mutually exclusive of course but I think part of this discussion has to do with how one uses personal horror storytelling while also including game structures that facilitate play and storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T13:19:34-07:00","id":1539656,"title":"","content":"There is at least one way of playing that I consider Wrong. I think I have mentioned a few times a story I was told by writer Bruce Baugh about a LARP he attended in which three Malkavian characters were going around, arms locked, and planting themselves in peoples' way while proclaiming &quot;we are a hedge!&quot; This is essentially just three people being a-holes and making everything difficult for everyone else just for their own childish amusement. Basically trolling. It's a violation of the gamer social compact, the first tenet of which is that everyone is there to have fun. And I despise that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T16:02:51-07:00","id":1539666,"title":"","content":"Outside of toxic behavoir i dont really consider any play style incorrect. I do think theirs a disconect with how the games are genrally played and how the publishers present them. Im not even convinced the hunger dice similate personal horror very well outside of specific circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T01:57:07-07:00","id":1539684,"title":"","content":"I think the thing about V:TM is that it's very much a comic book in the Batman sense. It can be VERY VERY serious but it can also be awesome and Pulpy.<br /> <br /> Blade and Underworld vs. Interview and Byzantium<br /> <br /> I think that people who try to make it SERIOUS AND DEEP by holding the Blade part in contempt have lost something essential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T11:16:49-07:00","id":1539714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539628#post1539628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(In hindsight, I really do wish Vampire and the other games had done more books devoted to specific genres and how to do them for your game. Like, this is the Horror genre, its tropes, and how to incorporate them into Vampire. And this is the Political Conspiracy/Mystery genre, this is Gothic Romance, etc. I think the closest we got was Wraith's Love Beyond Death and Mage's Dark Adventure.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You kind of do get this with Vampire: The Victorian Age, with treatises on the Gothic Horror genre, its tropes, and how they can be incorporated in a Vampire game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T15:02:11-07:00","id":1539721,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to go ahead and say it...<br /> <br /> In my humble opinion, I feel Justin Achilli and all of his imitators did a lot of damage to the Vampire: The Masquerade IP in the long run","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 08-02-2024, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T18:50:00-07:00","id":1539726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539721#post1539721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just going to go ahead and say it...<br /> <br /> In my humble opinion, I feel Justin Achilli and all of his imitators did a lot of damage to the Vampire: The Masquerade IP in the long run</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the third edition of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> is, I would still argue, the best single rulebook for the game, presenting a strong and cohesive view of what <i>Vampire</i> is supposed to be, and about 85% of the book was written by Justin Achilli.<br /> <br /> There are some serious problems which arose from his tenure as developer of the game; I would suggest that these were the following:<br /> <br /> <b>The One True Way:</b> The starting point for revised edition was to pull together all the disparate odds and ends which had accrued over previous years. So, you have a rulebook which contains rules for all thirteen clans, all main disciplines, Merits and Flaws, Paths of Enlightenment, and then supplements which take the same approach, leaving you feeling that you're playing the same game, regardless of which books you are reading (pick up<i> A World of Darkness</i> and <i>Ghouls: Fatal Addiction</i>, and read them alongside each other; they don't read like they reference the same universe, let alone the same game). But this desire for cohesiveness ends up in rants about trenchcoats and katanas, and the implication that there are wrong ways to play the game. Compare <i>Chicago by Night</i> with <i>New York by Night</i> and you can see how this approach risks just making everything boring. <br /> <br /> <b>Metaplot: </b>When the concept of metaplot was introduced in <i>Nights of Prophecy</i> it had to be explained to the reader, because the average player or Storyteller had no idea what this represented (it had been discussed, often forcefully, on Usenet for a few years by that point, but most gamers were not on alt.games.whitewolf). Metaplot is a bad idea for lots of reasons, but primarily because it exists for people who are readers and spectators, rather than for people who are players. And it feeds into...<br /> <br /> <b>The Supplement Treadmill:</b> This one wasn't Justin Achilli's fault, but a significant issue during his era in charge. There was, at this time, a great pressure to push out more game supplements, with more regularity. <i>Vampire</i>, during the revised-era, was seeing a book per month. This led to all kinds of junk being put into press. Firstly, you ended up with books coming into print which seemed good on paper, but were worthless in practice - I don't think there is a single worthwhile, usage sentence in <i>Succubus Club: Dead Man's Party</i>. Secondly, the volume of working coming out is too quick for the development cycle to properly manage, and has a demand for the written word which exceeds the talent pool available. One massive issue coming out of this was verbiage; there were many books that were twice as long as they needed to be, ending up filled up with words for the sake of words. It would be an interesting exercise to see how page count crept up over time...<br /> <br /> <b>Rock Star Writers:</b> Prior to White Wolf, RPG writers were uncool nerds. White Wolf was in the right place at the right time, surfed the wave of the emerging Internet to put writers and creators in touch with fans (alt.games.whitewolf again) and created personal fandoms around creators which never really existed before or since. Writers, and more crucially developers would be told literally every day how great they were, and how every decision they were making was the right one for the game (until Jess Heinig took over <i>Mage: the Ascension</i>; and, again, this was not his fault, but no-one knew that at the time). This created a toxic fandom, which did not accept any dissent in relation to the rock stars, nor exposure of their misbehaviour (one of the great scandals was the Matt McFarland cover-up of 2003; before the &quot;me too&quot; movement, it was incredibly difficult to reveal the misconduct of particular individuals in the RPG industry). And, of course, an industry where criticism is actively opposed is going to end up with quality issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T19:17:30-07:00","id":1539816,"title":"","content":"I'll take your word about what you said about Justin Achilli Matt. Still there was some good stuff during his time at White-Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T01:31:53-07:00","id":1539833,"title":"","content":"I dont think you can blame one guy for the issues wod has with diversity. I think a lot of it actually boils down to cultural. Wod grew very quickly during the 90's and this size didnt really match an awareness of it as a commercial product.<br /> at the same time toxicity in the true way mindset was never pushed back on in the community. Its only really getting pushback now its actually becoming disruptive within the community.<br /> <br /> As a side i dont think paradox are deliberatly doing this, its more they're going back to the well with old stuff and the culture combined with the mechanics of v5 means misery porn saturates the setting and i think the purists have misinterpreted product mismangement as deliberate design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T04:14:23-07:00","id":1539839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539074#post1539074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean yeah that's what the video basically says. Sure the setting is dark and brooding but it also has plenty of goofy shit underneath the surface so it's better to embrace it. For added variety if nothing else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean yeah this is a gross oversimplification for cometic effect on the video's part. But this video isn't a meant to be a lore primer, it's basically a Welcome to &quot;WOD, here's what you can expect in a game&quot; both serious and goofy.</div> </div> </div> </div> When it comes to presenting a setting as Mad, Bad and Dangerous to Know, nothing beats the ability to flip from WHAT WE DO IN THE SHADOWS to THE HUNGER at short notice: helps keep the audience in their toes!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T04:22:57-07:00","id":1539840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539150#post1539150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, because I became immortal to dress in flannel. - Toreador</div> </div> </div> </div>TOREADOR II - \u201cNo, you became a Toreador to pretend that Basic Black with everything was a pinnacle of sartorial bliss, not an ongoing national tragedy and a cry for help.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T14:50:26-07:00","id":1539888,"title":"","content":"Malkavian -&quot; Some people can wear spandex properly and sadly that is not you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T21:42:35-07:00","id":1539915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool#post1538996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren\u2019t just tormented with generic angst and tragic backstory. No, worse, being a vampire is not cool. The protagonists of these three stories are some of the whiniest most unlikable vampires in fiction. So much so that Louis of Interview with a Vampire would say they\u2019re a bunch of losers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof.... that is a burn. That is a fucking burn. XD<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool#post1538996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cFine Print\u201d follows the world\u2019s dumbest Ventrue. Duke negotiates a contract with his sire before his Embrace, apparently assuming this is legally enforceable, and is obnoxious the entire way through. He also doesn\u2019t bother to learn that he can\u2019t eat food beforehand, that sunlight forces him to sleep, or that vampires like him need special kinds of blood to drink. This probably my favorite of the stories and Duke really should have been staked for the Sun on his first night.</div> </div> </div> </div>How was even selected for embrace? Uhhh....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool#post1538996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cThe Land of Milk and Honey\u201d follows a vegan Toreador Anarch who runs a commune of blood harvesters that raise their own food as well as animals. Leigh is among the absolute worst kind of lifestyle advocates who basically keeps her subordinates as animals to harvest but insists on it being the more humane alternative. Its blackly funny that other Kindred seem to think of her as an extreme pro-vegan type in-universe but listening to her ramble on about her ideology the entire time just makes me want to see the Sabbat arrive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, who is she harvesting blood from? Animals? Humans? Other cainites?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool#post1538996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have no torment from the fact they\u2019re good people forced to be evil by hunger or circumstance.... These guys are like the obnoxious lady at the supermarket being turned into Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the true horror of of Embraces. When Embraces no longer chosen from the best candidates, but instead chosen from the most average of mortals. Karens and what so. <br /> <br /> That actually might be hell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28432-misskaos22","name":"MissKaos22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28432_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T04:42:50-07:00","id":1539920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539888#post1539888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malkavian -&quot; Some people can wear spandex properly and sadly that is not you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> \u201cIf I still had a pulse, I would live only to prove you wrong: anyway, you\u2019re still going to eat your words, no spitting, only swallow.\u201d<br /> <br /> - PULLS OUT MOBILE -<br /> <br /> \u201cEDNA, dearest - no no no, you still owe me a favour and capes are still The Coolest, my mind is still made up and you will only change it through actual brain surgery - Edna, Edna, FAVOUR. Alright, thank you, somebody wearing a baseball cap with a dressing gown has just called my legs into question and this aggression will not stand!<br /> <br /> No, really, MY legs - I know, right? - anyway, I need the best skintight so I came to The Very Best. NO, you\u2019re still dead wrong about capes but you\u2019re still The Best - so sorry, The Very Best - at everything else.<br /> <br /> Mmm-hm, measurements still the same, I keep in shape (Liquid diet): no no, black should be a feature, not the whole colour scheme - of course I won\u2019t wear it with a cape, ours is an honourable disagreement despite - thank you, thank you dearest darling bestest one - Saturday night\u2019s just right.<br /> <br /> Kisses kisses, ciao for now!\u201d<br /> <br /> - HANGS UP - <br /> <br /> Just you wait, Mooncalf, just you wait.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T10:51:51-07:00","id":1539932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539726#post1539726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, the third edition of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> is, I would still argue, the best single rulebook for the game, presenting a strong and cohesive view of what <i>Vampire</i> is supposed to be, and about 85% of the book was written by Justin Achilli.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed completely and when Achilli has other people to keep him in check, you can get some truly good stuff like the Revised and V20 corebooks or the OG Clanbook Giovanni from Second Edition.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you could run an ideal VTM game in any style with just the Revised corebook (and maybe the Storytellers Companion book that came with the ST Screen if you want more detailed rules on weaponry and vehicles and some of the more prominent minor bloodlines like the Samedi or Daughters of Cacophony)<br /> <br /> V20 is even more comprehensive but that is a double-edged sword because it's so damn comprehensive and that can overwhelm a newbie sometimes.<br /> <br /> If I were to introduce a newbie to Vampire, I'd give them just the Revised corebook and maybe tell them to stay the fuck away from V5 (at its absolute best, V5 is basically the WoD equivalent of D&amp;D 4e as far as I'm concerned)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T13:42:38-07:00","id":1539942,"title":"","content":"Malkavian: &quot; So Mr. Duke according to what I've seen of your actions thus far, I think your sire is playing a long bad joke on you or he lost a best with the Prince on how long you would last before you get staked on left to see the sun.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T06:55:48-07:00","id":1539988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539942#post1539942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malkavian: &quot; So Mr. Duke according to what I've seen of your actions thus far, I think your sire is playing a long bad joke on you or he lost a best with the Prince on how long you would last before you get staked on left to see the sun.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Jokes on you, Mooncalf, my sire WON that bet and my papa was an EARL.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T23:54:18-07:00","id":1540034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539684#post1539684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the thing about V:TM is that it's very much a comic book in the Batman sense. It can be VERY VERY serious but it can also be awesome and Pulpy.<br /> <br /> Blade and Underworld vs. Interview and Byzantium<br /> <br /> I think that people who try to make it SERIOUS AND DEEP by holding the Blade part in contempt have lost something essential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best chronicles are able to blend those two extremes in a way that is fun for their gaming group. I think players want the feel of stories like Interview and Byzantium while wanting the fun of Blade and Underworld. They want to experience the best scenes from Coppola's Dracula, Lost Boys, Near Dark, Count Yorga, Innocent Blood, and any other number of movies. The exact mix is always going to differ from gaming group to gaming group.<br /> <br /> Sourcebooks should be about giving STs tools so they can create the kind of game that works best for their players. Not trying to police badwrongfun at someone else's gaming table.<br /> <br /> I have met many players who approach the game in ways that make me barf. My gift to them is that I do not play in their games because not only would it not be fun for me, I would make it not fun for them.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I noticed that the best way to improve other people's games is to run your games (or sometimes just your character) the way you like. If there is any merit to it, other players will appreciate how your games are different and better than what they've had. And then they will steal what they like and won't copy the things that don't do anything for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 08-10-2024, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T08:39:40-07:00","id":1540042,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think it's great that parts of the community are reclaiming fangpions as a viable gameplay style, and I honestly think I see the word used more without malice these days. My main issue with WoD5 is simply that it brings up societal issues and then goes out of it's why to imply that fighting them is a waste of time.<br /> <br /> Hell I look at V5 Anarchs and I honestly don't get what they're saying about society. Something about how those opposing injustice invariably devolve into cruelty or something? At the very least the Carthian's dark side seemed to be about the realities of being the one in charge.<br /> <br /> I prefer the version of WoD aimed at my parents to the one aimed at me because it seems to actually want you to fight for the cause. It says that the world is shit, and that you're right to be angry, and understands that while you shouldn't go out and shoot the perpetrators that pretending to be a monster who is ripping them apart can be cathartic if approached with some maturity.<br /> <br /> To be the issue is that WoD5 can get too close to 'oppose politely or you're the baddy', whereas older books can be more 'be disruptive, eventually they'll have to listen'. But a lot of that might be the Werewolf fan in me talking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T10:07:15-07:00","id":1540049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539932#post1539932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to introduce a newbie to Vampire, I'd give them just the Revised corebook and maybe tell them to stay the fuck away from V5 (at its absolute best, V5 is basically the WoD equivalent of D&amp;D 4e as far as I'm concerned)</div> </div> </div> </div>D&amp;D 4e had way more good and exceptional points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T11:40:15-07:00","id":1540055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540049#post1540049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> D&amp;D 4e had way more good and exceptional points.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, you are correct.<br /> <br /> V5 at its absolute best is still shittier than 4e at its worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T17:37:54-07:00","id":1540070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540042#post1540042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think it's great that parts of the community are reclaiming fangpions as a viable gameplay style, and I honestly think I see the word used more without malice these days. My main issue with WoD5 is simply that it brings up societal issues and then goes out of it's why to imply that fighting them is a waste of time.<br /> <br /> Hell I look at V5 Anarchs and I honestly don't get what they're saying about society. Something about how those opposing injustice invariably devolve into cruelty or something? At the very least the Carthian's dark side seemed to be about the realities of being the one in charge.<br /> <br /> I prefer the version of WoD aimed at my parents to the one aimed at me because it seems to actually want you to fight for the cause. It says that the world is shit, and that you're right to be angry, and understands that while you shouldn't go out and shoot the perpetrators that pretending to be a monster who is ripping them apart can be cathartic if approached with some maturity.<br /> <br /> To be the issue is that WoD5 can get too close to 'oppose politely or you're the baddy', whereas older books can be more 'be disruptive, eventually they'll have to listen'. But a lot of that might be the Werewolf fan in me talking.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know the a bit off topic here since this is supposed to be a VTM thread but post like this brings this section of Werewolf the esstals preview I got:<br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ciUiIXX.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/ciUiIXX.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/ciUiIXX.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> In short the future is uncertain but it's for the new genration of heros to rise up to the challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T12:25:47-07:00","id":1540140,"title":"","content":"A Toreador Vegan???? that is painful to read and yes I can see my guy making a deal with the Sabbat to strike that place and not feel all that bad as he really doesn't like that clan in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T08:43:13-07:00","id":1540627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540042#post1540042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think it's great that parts of the community are reclaiming fangpions as a viable gameplay style, and I honestly think I see the word used more without malice these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this because the playstyle in and of itself is appealing, or because it's become a rallying point for people opposed to the vibe and themes V5's writers chose to put on the forefront? Because...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My main issue with WoD5 is simply that it brings up societal issues and then goes out of it's why to imply that fighting them is a waste of time. </div> </div> </div>That's...always been there. The &quot;punk&quot; in &quot;Gothic punk&quot; is something of a trojan horse for deeper exploration of institutional momentum, and the impotence of an individual to effect change in the context of aggressively individualist society ruled by &quot;fuck you I got mine&quot; mentality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell I look at V5 Anarchs and I honestly don't get what they're saying about society. Something about how those opposing injustice invariably devolve into cruelty or something? </div> </div> </div>Again, always been there.<br /> <br /> What changed between now and past editions' &quot;out with the old tyrant, in with the new&quot; cyclical portrayal of the Anarchs, was V20 when Onyx Path decided basically out of nowhere to reframe them as the setting's designated antiheroes -- putting the fractures in the community in the first place. Prior to then, the Anarchs had always been a joke faction -- lost boys hellraisers when no skin's in the game, libertarians pretending to be revolutionaries when skin's in the game, worse tyrants than anything the Camarilla could bring to bear when they're running the table.<br /> <br /> It was just the unfortunate case not everyone was in on the joke. Made it easier for certain writers to insert their personal political biases into the setting and run with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I prefer the version of WoD aimed at my parents to the one aimed at me because it seems to actually want you to fight for the cause. </div> </div> </div>Which version was that? Because the earlier editions wore their postmodernism on the sleeve: world's shit and run by superpredators whose lackeys will see you destroyed long before they learn your name -- if ever -- and the best you can do is your own thing for as long as you can before invariably gazing too deeply into the abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T09:29:05-07:00","id":1540633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540627#post1540627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's...always been there. The &quot;punk&quot; in &quot;Gothic punk&quot; is something of a trojan horse for deeper exploration of institutional momentum, and the impotence of an individual to effect change in the context of aggressively individualist society ruled by &quot;fuck you I got mine&quot; mentality.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also inaccurate because it basically misses that Punk fiction tends to derive its spiritual themes from noir fiction. For an example, HELLBLAZER and the works of Grant Morrison are definitely punk occult comic books. However, the point of Hellblazer isn't, &quot;John Constantine doesn't do shit and accomplishes nothing.&quot; No, the point of Hellblazer is that John Constantine thumbs his nose at authority every fucking chance he gets and manages to do so at heavy cost. Like the private detective, there's no actual fixing the corrupt police and systems of power. However, you can make a small amount of good or at least fuck with the bad(der) guys.<br /> <br /> Bad World of Darkness Plot:<br /> <br /> The player characters are hired by the Prince to kidnap someone. They find out it's a little girl. They turn over the little girl to the Prince and she's eaten. They collect their fee.<br /> <br /> Good World of Darkness Plot:<br /> <br /> The player characters are hired by the Prince to kidnap someone. They find out it's a little girl. They raise hell on Earth to try to protect her. They might succeed or might fail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What changed between now and past editions' &quot;out with the old tyrant, in with the new&quot; cyclical portrayal of the Anarchs, was V20 when Onyx Path decided basically out of nowhere to reframe them as the setting's designated antiheroes -- putting the fractures in the community in the first place. Prior to then, the Anarchs had always been a joke faction -- lost boys hellraisers when no skin's in the game, libertarians pretending to be revolutionaries when skin's in the game, worse tyrants than anything the Camarilla could bring to bear when they're running the table. </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs have never meant to be stupid. That was a product of LOS ANGELES BY NIGHT utterly derailing them. They were meant to be flawed but a lighter shade of black than the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> To go with &quot;World of Darkness is just Cyberpunk 2020 with fangs&quot;<br /> <br /> The Camarilla Elders are the corpos and absolute evil but the people you work for. The Anarchs are the cyberpunks/street samurai who oppose the corpos but still end up mostly part of the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T10:12:43-07:00","id":1540635,"title":"","content":"Golconda existed for a reason, and there was also a reason for it to be thoroughly good in First Edition.<br /> <br /> In earlier editions the game was all about sticking to the Man and actually accepting the challenge and go do some actual good in this shitty world. And the Anarchs were the obvious heroic faction from day one.<br /> <br /> Most groups liked to explore the darkness. The game was expanded to accommodate many play styles. After a while the Cam and the Sabbat got a lot of development. But the original game cycle was all about doing the Revolution one step at a time and actually eventually succeed.<br /> <br /> Of course, as a setting the game must keep the bleak <i>status quo</i>, but that's simply setup for the actual game at your table.<br /> <br /> That's one of the reasons I don't like to get everything good in the setting and make it grey and dubious at best. This is to miss the whole point that overcoming this shitty society is actually possible, and the only thing keeping it from being better is the interest of those in power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T10:32:26-07:00","id":1540636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540627#post1540627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this because the playstyle in and of itself is appealing, or because it's become a rallying point for people opposed to the vibe and themes V5's writers chose to put on the forefront? Because...</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the person, but the style has always been appealing. Really the argument against it has always loosely been the same as the 'pink mohican vs mirrorshades' arguments in cyberpunk games.<br /> <br /> It probably helps that the current trend seems to be a move towards more hopeful settings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's...always been there. The &quot;punk&quot; in &quot;Gothic punk&quot; is something of a trojan horse for deeper exploration of institutional momentum, and the impotence of an individual to effect change in the context of aggressively individualist society ruled by &quot;fuck you I got mine&quot; mentality. </div> </div> </div>I thought the 'punk' aspect was the rage against the system. Yes you're weak and can't topple the power structures that exist but you can still do <i>something</i>. The Anarchs can't topple the Camarilla but they always seem to be there trying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, always been there.<br /> <br /> What changed between now and past editions' &quot;out with the old tyrant, in with the new&quot; cyclical portrayal of the Anarchs, was V20 when Onyx Path decided basically out of nowhere to reframe them as the setting's designated antiheroes -- putting the fractures in the community in the first place. Prior to then, the Anarchs had always been a joke faction -- lost boys hellraisers when no skin's in the game, libertarians pretending to be revolutionaries when skin's in the game, worse tyrants than anything the Camarilla could bring to bear when they're running the table.<br /> <br /> It was just the unfortunate case not everyone was in on the joke. Made it easier for certain writers to insert their personal political biases into the setting and run with it. </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs weren't a joke faction early on, yes they were underdogs but they were the only serious opposition to the Camarilla. That changed when the Sabbat went from a semi-legendary group of Boogeymen to a rival sect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which version was that? Because the earlier editions wore their postmodernism on the sleeve: world's shit and run by superpredators whose lackeys will see you destroyed long before they learn your name -- if ever -- and the best you can do is your own thing for as long as you can before invariably gazing too deeply into the abyss. </div> </div> </div>I was honestly thinking more of Werewolf and Mage, where latter editions made 'winning' more likely. Not actually likely, but certainly feasible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T11:43:10-07:00","id":1540641,"title":"","content":"My take on the subject is you were never supposed to BEAT the Elders.<br /> <br /> But you could FIGHT them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T13:33:14-07:00","id":1540651,"title":"","content":"And hope to survive the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T14:10:04-07:00","id":1540656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540641#post1540641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on the subject is you were never supposed to BEAT the Elders.<br /> <br /> But you could FIGHT them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. But you could beat the inner beast and be a decent person.<br /> <br /> The horror of the game - and of both fictional and real society - is that at the end of the day, the world don't need to be shitty. It really is, at the end, a lack of trying to do better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T14:37:24-07:00","id":1540657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540633#post1540633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is also inaccurate because it basically misses that Punk fiction tends to derive its spiritual themes from noir fiction...Like the private detective, there's no actual fixing the corrupt police and systems of power. However, you can make a small amount of good or at least fuck with the bad(der) guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence &quot;the best you can do is your own thing as long as you can, before you inevitably lose (by either selling out, falling to wassail, or meeting Final Death)&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's a far, <i>far</i> cry from the current &quot;darkly heroic&quot; framing of Anarchs by certain parts of the community. &quot;Fighting the Man&quot; has always been part of the setting and theme, sure, but that doesn't mean it's an heroic or even antiheroic conflict by default against designated villains.<br /> <br /> People need to remember this is a game about nocturnal sociopaths with a compulsion to hunt and kill humans that extends beyond the need to simply survive, with a fight-or-flight instinct that turns them into Doom Guy at the drop of a hat. There's no heroism or antiheroism there, just self-delusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bad World of Darkness Plot:<br /> <br /> The player characters are hired by the Prince to kidnap someone. They find out it's a little girl. They turn over the little girl to the Prince and she's eaten. They collect their fee.<br /> <br /> Good World of Darkness Plot:<br /> <br /> The player characters are hired by the Prince to kidnap someone. They find out it's a little girl. They raise hell on Earth to try to protect her. They might succeed or might fail. </div> </div> </div>No. Just, no.<br /> <br /> Good World of Darkness plot:<br /> The player characters are hired by the Prince to kidnap someone. They find out it's a little girl, then they're led down a rabbit hole of conflicting interests, motives, and players involved that muddy the moral and ethical waters to such a degree there's no clear right or wrong action despite surface-level analysis. And they have to figure out the <i>best possible</i> way to navigate the clusterfuck in which they find themselves and keep their necks intact, to whatever end that may be.<br /> <br /> Bad World of Darkness plot:<br /> The player characters are hired by the Prince to kidnap someone. They find out it's a little girl. There's no nuance, moral quandry, or deeper levels to this, it's just purely superficial with one &quot;right&quot; way to resolve the conflict towards which players are shepherded regardless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Anarchs have never meant to be stupid. </div> </div> </div>I'm without doubt they were never meant to be stupid. They just happened to be written that way out of lack of self-awareness, which later writers would realize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Anarchs are the cyberpunks/street samurai who oppose the corpos <u><b>but still end up mostly part of the system</b></u>. </div> </div> </div>And there it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540636#post1540636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the person, but the style has always been appealing. Really the argument against it has always loosely been the same as the 'pink mohican vs mirrorshades' arguments in cyberpunk games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure there are plenty of folks who like that style of play, but again: is its resurgence genuine, or is it a rallying point for V5 critics?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It probably helps that the current trend seems to be a move towards more hopeful settings. </div> </div> </div>Is it really more hopeful, or is it just hyperfocused on the levels of play in which player characters can have influence?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Anarchs can't topple the Camarilla but they always seem to be there trying. </div> </div> </div>This is what I'm calling out. The Anarchs may have deluded &quot;true believer&quot; neonates in their ranks, but for the ancillae and elders among them, it's not about toppling extant power structures. It's about seizing extant power structures for themselves. That's why the Anarchs are a joke faction, they're just a more palatable flavor of Camarilla. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Anarchs weren't a joke faction early on, yes they were underdogs but they were the only serious opposition to the Camarilla. </div> </div> </div>Loyal -- or outright controlled -- opposition to the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T07:14:57-07:00","id":1540702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540656#post1540656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. But you could beat the inner beast and be a decent person.<br /> <br /> The horror of the game - and of both fictional and real society - is that at the end of the day, the world don't need to be shitty. It really is, at the end, a lack of trying to do better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beating the inner beast is a day to day struggle and the world will always demand compromises of a Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T07:19:37-07:00","id":1540703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good World of Darkness plot:<br /> The player characters are hired by the Prince to kidnap someone. They find out it's a little girl, then they're led down a rabbit hole of conflicting interests, motives, and players involved that muddy the moral and ethical waters to such a degree there's no clear right or wrong action despite surface-level analysis. And they have to figure out the <i>best possible</i> way to navigate the clusterfuck in which they find themselves and keep their necks intact, to whatever end that may be.<br /> <br /> Bad World of Darkness plot:<br /> The player characters are hired by the Prince to kidnap someone. They find out it's a little girl. There's no nuance, moral quandry, or deeper levels to this, it's just purely superficial with one &quot;right&quot; way to resolve the conflict towards which players are shepherded regardless. </div> </div> </div>No, just no.<br /> <br /> Because if there's no sense the PCs actually want to do the right thing then there's no fucking point in Humanity. The choice is endangering themselves, their loved ones, and their power in the city.<br /> <br /> The &quot;moral quandry&quot; implies that vampires are somehow equally moral in their decisions versus bad decisions vs. worse decisions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is what I'm calling out. The Anarchs may have deluded &quot;true believer&quot; neonates in their ranks, but for the ancillae and elders among them, it's not about toppling extant power structures. It's about seizing extant power structures for themselves. That's why the Anarchs are a joke faction, they're just a more palatable flavor of Camarilla. </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that &quot;seizing power for themselves&quot; isn't hypocrisy for a lot of low level Anarchs. The Anarchs include a bunch of idealists but plenty of them make no pretenses that their reason for hating the Camarilla is the fact they want to do whatever the fuck they want.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of street gang influence in the Anarchs in addition to communist, socialist, and justice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Loyal -- or outright controlled -- opposition to the Camarilla. </div> </div> </div>Was this a product of Revised? Because the Anarchs murdered and overthrew Princes in Chicago by Night, Los Angeles by Night, and The Anarchs Cookbook. They're not loyal in the fucking slightest.<br /> <br /> They just get considered Camarilla because the Camarilla considers all vampires a part of it.<br /> <br /> Even so, the Prince will go out of his way to make reasons up to murder Anarchs. ASHES TO ASHES had Sheriff try to burn down a Rave full of Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T07:38:26-07:00","id":1540704,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a> <br /> Posting this video as i want to show that humans themselves are already failing at an easier form of controlling the &quot;beast&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ms2BvRbjOYo\" data-code=\"ms2BvRbjOYo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ms2BvRbjOYo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> and additional to that, while reaching Golconda was a &quot;goal&quot; in the early editions, I have never heard of any PC succeeding and only a few even trying. In the lore Golconda is this almost mythical state of enlightenment. It's said to grant peace, control over bloodlust, in a way freedom from the curse of vampirism itself (walking in the sun etc.), but whether any vampire has truly reached Golconda is still a mystery. The most famous figure associated with it is Saulot, who some believe achieved this state before his... &quot;death&quot;. The ambiguity around Golconda is part of what makes it intriguing, but whether it's a real, attainable goal or just another false hope for the cursed, the truth remains elusive.<br /> <br /> It is a playstyle that i seldom see, which is kind of sad. Still would not say that it is even close in terms of default. Not saying it is wrong to play that way, i would love to see it.<br /> <br /> And on the whole question @ all<br /> There is no wrong way to play the game, WoD should be a generalist system/world imho. All playstyles of urban fantasy should be supported.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T10:02:33-07:00","id":1540709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540702#post1540702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beating the inner beast is a day to day struggle and the world will always demand compromises of a Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is doable, that's my point.<br /> <br /> The struggle isn't easy, and vampiric society will make it all the more hard. But it is doable.<br /> <br /> Not only that, it is meant to be the main goal in the actual early editions, because what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a> describes is actually Revised, by no means this utter bleakness is First or even Second edition.<br /> <br /> In those, doing actual good is meant to be hard, but doable, and the grey morality comes from how hard it is to stick to the right thing, not from everything being kinda wrong because the world is grimdark and everybody sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 08-19-2024, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T14:09:58-07:00","id":1540725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540703#post1540703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if there's no sense the PCs actually want to do the right thing then there's no fucking point in Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, most players do not find it fun to roleplay the whole &quot;Beast I am lest a beast I become&quot; that is supposedly the heart of the game. Some players do indeed like that, but let's face it, a lot of fun with RPG is a power fantasy element. Too much concern over Humanity, or too many scenes that put Humanity in jeopardy can suck the fun out of the game. They want that to be an occasional spice used in the game, not the main thing done. <br /> <br /> Usually players decide there is a certain level of Humanity they are comfortable for their PC (and the &quot;right&quot; level of Humanity can change from PC to PC for many players). Anything above that, they don't care that much for morality checks. They only start caring when it involves things that drop them past the level they like for their style of play.<br /> <br /> Some players do want their PC to be fairly high Humanity, say 7 or above. Usually the PCs that slot there are vampires not overly concerned about the &quot;typical&quot; plots and activities of most Vampire games. They aren't concerned about their PCs becoming powerful politically, fighting any combat, sect wars, etc. They're interested in other aspects of the setting. They'll typically make the &quot;right&quot; moral choice because they'll avoid most moral dilemmas entirely. They won't turn over a kidnapped child to the Prince to be eaten because they have no reason to do so in the first place. The Prince simply cannot offer them anything that is meaningful for them. There may be moments when such PCs do face a moral dilemma that tests them, but such moments are rare and typically have meaning. And if they are not rare, but common, they tend to get pissed off at the ST for constantly targeting them to lose Humanity when all they want to do is have fun (their way) roleplaying a fairly moral vampire.<br /> <br /> Other players don't want to be moral monsters, but are perfectly happy to settle at a noticeably lower level of Humanity that allows them to accomplish most of their goals. They are happy to settle on Humanity 5. They don't intend for their PCs to be murderers, but they want to build power, increase their status, and defend themselves when necessary. These PCs often start with much higher Humanity. When I ST, I typically ask my players what level of Humanity they would be comfortable at for most of the game. If they start at 7, but know their playing style is going to drop that to 5, I ask them how often do they want to do roll a Conscience check that is above their &quot;target&quot; of 5. I get all sorts of answers. Many players do not want to roleplay out any kind of remorse or moral drama. They are find having their Humanity drop 7 to 6 and then to 5 automatically. Only once they reach the level they feel is &quot;appropriate&quot; for their character, do they want real Conscience checks. Other players tell me they want to decide so to give them an option to do so when I think a check is required, and they'll tell me if that situation would be fun for them. Some players always want it. It just depends on how much this aspect of the game is fun for them.<br /> <br /> More rarely, the PC intends to be a real thorough going bastard. They know their character is going to fall to 3-4, maybe even lower. I give them the same options of determining whether they roll above that level of Humanity. Typically such players don't find it fun to roleplay through Humanity checks. They know their character is a ruthless bastard and find roleplaying fake conscience checks to just be in the way of having fun.<br /> <br /> Typically the only time I see players really enjoy playing through preserving their humanity is when their PC is at a middle group. They have a comfortable level of Humanity, but really don't want to go below 5, and legitimate scenes that force them to make a decision at that point of Humanity (but not before) is something they can enjoy. As long as they truly make the decision in a scene they think is appropriate for their character. But like the first group, they get upset if they think the ST is purposefully creating plot to force them to make rolls, rather than something they find as organic.<br /> <br /> But in no case do I see players wanting &quot;to do the right thing&quot; regardless for their PC. That's not why they play Vampire. If they want to have PCs where they always make the morally good choice, they typically will play some other RPG setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540703#post1540703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not loyal in the fucking slightest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not the Anarchs are any kind of &quot;controlled&quot; or &quot;loyal&quot; opposition really depends on what kind of Anarchs you are talking about, and the expectations of the individual player.<br /> <br /> I would argue most Anarchs in the game, and most PC Anarchs, just tend to want to get rid of a &quot;bad&quot; Prince (who makes fun of them and does not treat them as favorites) and put in a &quot;good' Prince instead (who makes fun of other characters, and treats them as favorites). Such characters could indeed be seen as &quot;controlled opposition&quot; by certain people (characters and players) because they aren't going against &quot;the system&quot;. Yeah, you can replace Lodin with Maldavis, but &quot;the system&quot; hasn't changed at all. You still have a Prince. You still have a Primogen. You still have the salon culture and Elysium and all of that.<br /> <br /> I think very few Anarchs actually want to abolish &quot;the system&quot; because neither the characters or players have any idea of what would replace it. If they do, it tends to be a fairly weak city domain democracy and some kind of Bill of Rights. But most of the &quot;Camarilla structure&quot; is left intact. There may be some actions a &quot;Prince&quot; or whatever you call the executive cannot do. There may be certain things that the masses can veto. Certain positions might be elected subject to recall or time limits. But it's all fairly tepid. There's still Justicars, still Conclaves, still an Inner Circle, still the Traditions, it just has some guard rails put on. Once again, there will be other characters or players who see this as not abolishing &quot;the system&quot;. Those Anarchs aren't &quot;real' Anarchs because they are not radical enough.<br /> <br /> To those characters and players, what they want to see are Anarchs who want to blow up the entire setting blown up and replace it by something else. They want to see Anarchs abolishing the Traditions, setting up pirate republics, organizing soviets or anarcho-syndicates, establish a theocracy, killing the Inner Council, legalizing diablerie against the elders, ignoring the clans and incorporating Caitiff into the power structure, or whatever. Because that is the only way &quot;the system&quot; can be overthrown. Unfortunately for them, the game has never really supported that. We get pitifully few ideas on what kind of specific agendas some Anarchs support as a replacement, and usually if players really want a game that is completely a non-Camarilla structure they just play Sabbat instead. So without some radical reimagining of the setting, the Anarchs simply cannot be anything other than a &quot;controlled&quot; opposition that simply swaps one Prince for another with no real changes.<br /> <br /> To other players, yeah, killing Lodin and putting Maldavis in place is hardcore Anarch, and they don't understand why these other characters (or players) don't get it. There's just little common ground between them.<br /> <br /> And I think that's fine. There's no reason why the Anarchs cannot have &quot;radicals&quot; like Salvador Garcia or Smiling Jack, &quot;moderates&quot; like Jeremy MacNeil or Hinds, &quot;reformers&quot; like Maldavis or Modius, and &quot;sell outs&quot; who comprise Camarilla loyalists who are sympathetic to the Anarchs. This kind of infighting and accusations of betrayal between factions is just normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T14:16:39-07:00","id":1540727,"title":"","content":"That always been my take on Anarch's Black Fox is that outside of not liking the Camarilla type of leadership at all. None of them have a good alternative to replace it and spend more time infighting and crippling themselves and overtime will become like Mommy and Daddy sire as my Malkavian would say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T14:28:30-07:00","id":1540729,"title":"","content":"Also, to a bunch of immortals, &quot;replace the corrupt leadership but not the system&quot; ISN'T a hypocritical stance.<br /> <br /> Nor is, &quot;Replace the corrupt leadership that hates me with corrupt leadership that likes me.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's like saying that overthrowing Team Lannister for Team Stark or Team Targaryen is hypocritical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T23:13:42-07:00","id":1540750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540729#post1540729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, to a bunch of immortals, &quot;replace the corrupt leadership but not the system&quot; ISN'T a hypocritical stance.<br /> <br /> Nor is, &quot;Replace the corrupt leadership that hates me with corrupt leadership that likes me.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's like saying that overthrowing Team Lannister for Team Stark or Team Targaryen is hypocritical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overthrowing the vastly more interesting and cool House for a House which either don't want the Iron Throne, and is alot less interesting, or is much less interesting and exciting to read about is not hypocritical. Its it however a very bad move.<br /> <br /> For remember: &quot;Men who are small can never stand tall while Lions still walk in the light.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T03:01:42-07:00","id":1540757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540727#post1540727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That always been my take on Anarch's Black Fox is that outside of not liking the Camarilla type of leadership at all. None of them have a good alternative to replace it and spend more time infighting and crippling themselves and overtime will become like Mommy and Daddy sire as my Malkavian would say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of it is bad writing that no one ever bothered to forward an alternative in-univere because the writers wanted to stick with the current V:TM system.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, they also have a good in-universe reason for it that vampires are inherently predatory and only function in tyrannical systems of absolute power.<br /> <br /> Princes are literally the product of Caine's law in The Book of Nod after all.<br /> <br /> We also know the Sabbat's system is identical except they mass blood-bond everyone to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T06:20:22-07:00","id":1540761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1540703#post1540703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, just no.<br /> <br /> Because if there's no sense the PCs actually want to do the right thing then there's no fucking point in Humanity. The choice is endangering themselves, their loved ones, and their power in the city.<br /> <br /> The &quot;moral quandry&quot; implies that vampires are somehow equally moral in their decisions versus bad decisions vs. worse decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so what happens if or when the &quot;little girl&quot; being kidnapped is a revenant? A Giovanni? A mortal descendent of the prince in bad circumstances, and the prince has zero interest just admitting a potential vulnerability to a group of neonates and instead wants to leverage it for a show of ruthlessness? Being raised as a sacrificial lamb to some infernalist cult? Hell, in V5 mechanics that little girl could be a touchstone and the prince's interest is in protecting her.<br /> <br /> The last one's by far the most interesting scenario. Do player characters oblige the prince, trusting they won't damage or destroy their own touchstone (once they discover the relevance of this kid to the prince), do it themselves as a strike against the prince's humanity, or act to protect the prince (and ultimately city) from themselves? Does the kid's current circumstances actually warrant intervention, and if so, might there be a preferable alternative to resolving the conflict?<br /> <br /> Of course, V5 is also the edition with the only solid mechanical justification for why an elder prince would just want to up and eat a little girl (ignoring the potential for Ventrue feeding preference to be children, but you didn't specify clan so I'm sticking to generalities).<br /> <br /> Those are the scenarios I could name off the top of my head in about thirty seconds, in which the act of kidnapping a little girl may not actually be the &quot;evil&quot; thing to do after all. It just <i>appears</i> to be as glimpsed through the fog of war, because player characters won't (and shouldn't) be privilege to that information on the outset -- it must be discovered through the course of the story.<br /> <br /> How about if the kid's possessed, a medium, has latent magical talent, or something else along those lines and poses a threat to the Masquerade -- and those around her -- for it? In this case, an occult-minded prince may have no interest in harming this child at all, or if they do it's in the form of raising them in preparation for the embrace when she reaches maturity. Either way, the end result is removing a potential threat to mortal and vampiric society and placing that kid in an environment where her abilities can be excised, suppressed, controlled, or developed -- or at least, keep them away from worse factions.<br /> <br /> This is grey all around, because the player characters must now openly speculate whether the prince is correct to have this child segregated, whether other parties might handle the situation better, or if the prince isn't just acting hastily (or on incomplete information) and the situation will course-correct on its own.<br /> <br /> And last but not least, what if we're dealing with a Damien Thorn/Michael Langdon/'baby Hitler&quot; situation where the kid's just straight fucking evil (superpowers not necessary), and the prince or one of the primogen with Auspex out the ears has foretold this kid <i>has</i> to be taken out of the picture for self-preservation. Doesn't even have to be an &quot;Antichrist&quot; type situation, maybe the kid just grows up to be the hunter that wipes out Elysium with a firebomb in ten years' time. Now we're not even talking about grey-on-black morality, we're talking about black-on-black for all the &quot;baby Hitler&quot; moral arguments to either side, in addition to relying on the accuracy of an elder's prophecy <i>and</i> the potential for this to become a self-fulfilling prophecy when or if the players' own actions are what ultimately cause the firebombing in ten years' time.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. You presented a scenario in which the prince uses PC's as procurers for their midnight snack. That's just a shitty, superficial, scenario with not nearly enough narrative meat to drive a plot or tie into a chronicle's narrative on its own -- <i>and</i> it doesn't hold up to scrutiny in the context of WoD's internal logic. After all, why the fuck would a prince send neonates to perform a rote task their own retinue and/or retainers could do on their own with far less chance of matters going awry, and far greater operational security?<br /> <br /> Simply put, a prince who would pull shit like this is a shitty prince -- and more on that later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd argue that &quot;seizing power for themselves&quot; isn't hypocrisy for a lot of low level Anarchs. The Anarchs include a bunch of idealists but plenty of them make no pretenses that their reason for hating the Camarilla is the fact they want to do whatever the fuck they want. </div> </div> </div>Including their turn on the tyranny bicycle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a lot of street gang influence in the Anarchs in addition to communist, socialist, and justice. </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and it's all pretense and self-delusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was this a product of Revised? Because the Anarchs murdered and overthrew Princes in Chicago by Night, Los Angeles by Night, and The Anarchs Cookbook. </div> </div> </div>And of those, who were competent princes that enjoyed alliance of their primogen, tolerance of neighboring princes, support of archons and justicars, and the approval of the inner council? Don't mistake the sect throwing a shitty prince who already had one foot out the door under the bus, for power or a lack of loyalty on Anarchs' part. It just means the Anarchs were the Camarilla's catspaw, witting or not, to take out a figurehead who was going to go sooner or later anyways.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to say Camarilla vampires are backbiting, arrogant, power hungry monsters. Nobody debates that. But, people who talk up Anarchs obsessively insist on one imagined aspect to the Camarilla lore by and large doesn't support -- they're <i>incompetent</i>. Anarchs don't have appeal unless the Camarilla is inept, and that's why players who like Anarchs must fixate on the Don Sebastians, Lodins, and LaCroixs of the setting -- as opposed to the Marcus Vitels (while he was still pretending to be Ventrue), Kevin Jacksons, and Mark Deckers of the setting. Because while those princes may not be nice people and certainly keep Anarchs on as tight a leash as possible, they're <i>competent</i>.<br /> <br /> And by all means must avoid at all costs mention of the Benison Hodges of the setting...as in those cases it's the Inner Council and Justicars themselves coming down on a prince hostile to Anarchs, specifically for their hostility to Anarchs.<br /> <br /> This is the core problem with Anarch &quot;normalization&quot;: by way of comparison, every other sect must be presented as a less-appealing option. And in this case, it mandates the 600-year-old vampiric society run by the apex predators' apex predators -- who for the most part are acutely aware of their own vulnerabilities -- who have had centuries to perfect statecraft, somehow abrogate their own skills, experience, and indeed common sense itself, to run that society in the least competent and sustainable way possible.<br /> <br /> And we know for fact that's how V5 canonized the post-Second Inquisition Camarilla, where instead of the likes of Lodin being the idiots who slip through the cracks of competency, it's the likes of Kevin Jackson being the competent administrators who slip through the cracks of idiocy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even so, the Prince will go out of his way to make reasons up to murder Anarchs. ASHES TO ASHES had Sheriff try to burn down a Rave full of Anarchs. </div> </div> </div><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1653_1724159537152_799\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1653\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1653\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1653&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-20-2024, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T12:55:37-07:00","id":1540969,"title":"","content":"I should add that our Anarch coterie has became more mercenary in there outlook as they approach there second century of existence and are willing to work with the Camarilla to get lore, boons and even a free pass in so and so domain as long they follow proper etqiuette.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T09:26:26-07:00","id":1541127,"title":"","content":"It's honestly kind of a shame that VTM turned against the idea of being &quot;cool&quot; at the exact wrong time. The goth and then vampire boom from 2000s well into the mid-2010s would have been great for sales if they stuck the landing after the industry crunch.<br /> <br /> The themes of Owod have only become more relevant in th 2020s, but the fact paradox doubled down on splitting the fanbase again means it probably isn't going to be able to strike that cord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T12:07:57-07:00","id":1541133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1541127#post1541127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's honestly kind of a shame that VTM turned against the idea of being &quot;cool&quot; at the exact wrong time. The goth and then vampire boom from 2000s well into the mid-2010s would have been great for sales if they stuck the landing after the industry crunch.<br /> <br /> The themes of Owod have only become more relevant in th 2020s, but the fact paradox doubled down on splitting the fanbase again means it probably isn't going to be able to strike that chord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox B flat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T19:45:39-07:00","id":1541159,"title":"","content":"While poking around the Noble Knight Games online store, I ran across the Black Dog Games imprint page. Like a lot of NKG's company pages, it included BDG's own description of itself and its mission statement when White Wolf created the brand around 1995.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Black Dog Game Factory is an imprint of White Wolf Publishing dedicated to producing artistic role-playing games and supplements for older, more mature readers. Black Dog intends to artistically pursue themes and issue that gaming has never been allowed to address, and transform gaming from an embarrassing hobby to something approaching art. </div> </div> </div>The phrase &quot;embarrassing hobby&quot; seems telling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T20:11:39-07:00","id":1541161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1541159#post1541159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While poking around the Noble Knight Games online store, I ran across the Black Dog Games imprint page. Like a lot of NKG's company pages, it included BDG's own description of itself and its mission statement when White Wolf created the brand around 1995.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The phrase &quot;embarrassing hobby&quot; seems telling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Condescending AND pretentious. Way to go, 90s White Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T22:32:54-07:00","id":1541167,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there was this weird sort of schism in WWGS at the time. On the one hand, you had a bunch of people, especially developers, who were long time gamers. Some had even done some work for TSR and were open AD&amp;D fans. On the other hand, you had this group who apparently felt they were too cool for that. This seems to have involved a number of people involved with the book publishing imprint and the magazine. Especially the magazine. I have never seen another game publisher house organ go so far out of its way to avoid talking about their own company's products. And when it rebranded as Inphobia, they doubled down on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T22:44:34-07:00","id":1541169,"title":"","content":"And I may be biased on this, but I don't remember any Black Dog release being exactly an example of mature approach to anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T23:09:57-07:00","id":1541172,"title":"","content":"Giovanni chronicles maybe (?)<br /> <br /> Anyway, this reminds me of the stuff the people at the forge wrote. Not saying that one did not leave a lasting impact, but i do feel that the bad (pretentiousness, toxicity, etc.) never left the hobby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T23:12:38-07:00","id":1541174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1541169#post1541169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I may be biased on this, but I don't remember any Black Dog release being exactly an example of mature approach to anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The Cainite Heresy</i> for <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i>? There was some art that was frankly quite juvenile, but the actual book itself is one of the best in the line, and presents a very mature review of heterodox beliefs.<br /> <br /> But the average quality of Black Dog books was quite poor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T23:51:18-07:00","id":1541176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1541169#post1541169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I may be biased on this, but I don't remember any Black Dog release being exactly an example of mature approach to anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charnel Houses of Europe is the shining exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T01:25:21-07:00","id":1541184,"title":"","content":"I think a big part of Black Dog's existence is because someone at WW really, really wanted to republish Human Occupied Landfill, Dirt Merchant Games' &quot;edgy&quot; satire of early 90s rpg tropes. It and its sole sourcebook, BUTTery HOLesomeness, are the only nonWoD releases the brand ever did. And as I said, I don't consider those actual games but snarky cynical efforts at satirizing early 90s rpgs. While &quot;art&quot; is subjective, I'm not sure they qualify in the way that blurb uses the term. <br /> <br /> The other aspect of its existence probably goes back to the original Brujah clanbook from 1992. One of the templates, the Rapper, used the word &quot;fuck&quot; in its character quote, and this apparently got some pushback from a few retailers. Because Vampire and the other games billed themselves as for &quot;mature readers&quot;, I think there was always this desire to try to get into what the American movie industry would consider &quot;hard R&quot; territory and talk frankly about &quot;adult themes&quot; using &quot;adult language&quot; but also having to deal with the reality that RPGs - being primarily sold through comic book stores at the time - were essentially an &quot;all ages&quot; hobby.<br /> <br /> Plus DC had created their Vertigo imprint just a few years earlier, making comics socially acceptable for alternative hipsters who didn't want to be associated with superhero nerds, and I think WWGS was always chasing that kind of reputation in the RPG sphere.<br /> <br /> As an aside, around this same time there was a book released called Generation Ecch, a very sarcastic and cynical overview of what was being touted as Gen X cultural tropes and interests (indie films, raves, 70s nostalgia, comics, etc.). Each chapter was opened with a page by alternative comic book maker Evan Dorkin, and the comic book chapter included a panel pointing out that most &quot;mature/adult&quot; comics just ended up being an excuse to swear a lot and draw naked breasts. And if you are familiar with most of the Black Dog label books, you know exactly why I brought that up.<br /> <br /> The initial wave was four books, one for each line. (God only knows what sort of book they'd have tried for Changeling if that line hasn't just been starting.) And I don't think any of them sold as well as was hoped.<br /> <br /> I've never fully read the entire Giovoni Chronicles, so I can't really say if they needed to be Black Dog or not. Honestly, I think insisting that the three follow up volumes also carry the label is what even kept the BD brand alive for the next few years.<br /> <br /> Freak Legion may as well be the poster child for what I mentioned earlier. It is almost entirely juvenile shock value for shock value's sake. <br /> <br /> Destiny's Price was a good idea, as a guide to inner city street life, the underground club scene, and gutterpunk culture is the sort of thing that would be useful for all of the WoD game lines. Unfortunately, this book is just sort of there. It never really got into the sort of detail about sex, drugs, and violence that would really justify this having the BD label. It feels like this was just going to be a regular book on the release schedule, got picked to be part of this project, and so the art department threw in a few pictures of S&amp;M strippers with bare breasts. (It wasn't really helped that shortly after it was released, films such as Trainspotting and Kids came out, making this instantly feel a little sanitized and dated.)<br /> <br /> Wraith's Spectres book was probably the one that came closest to deserving the Black Dog brand. Wraith was already a somewhat dark game that rewarded a type of roleplaying based on delving into what made your character tick and what baggage they carried around. With Spectres, you had that compounded by a massive amount of nihilism that I think is best left to players with a certain level of emotional maturity.<br /> <br /> Montreal by Night always felt like it was using the BD label as a marketing gimmick. It really didn't need it, but &quot;Oooooh, it's a Sabbat city, come look at how eeeeeevil and wicked they are!&quot; Plus some gratuitous human toilets.<br /> <br /> Clanbook Baali really has no good reason to exist. While half of the book does have some interesting ideas about prehistoric elder gods, it also wastes time with juvenile shock material (including really gross opening fiction that feels like it was written to appeal to the National Association of Marlan Brando Look-Alikes).<br /> <br /> The Cainite Heresy probably didn't really need the label but got it mainly because of the focus on religious sects and its reexaminations of the Path of Evil Revelations. The fact that it was written by two skilled authors, Ken Hite and R Sean Borgstrom, certainly helped elevate its quality.<br /> <br /> Finally, Charnel Houses of Europe. I think this is the only book that ever really lived up to the label's potential. It is a serious look at a serious subject, and endeavors to use roleplaying games as a teaching tool to help educate people about the Holocaust. It was a deeply personal project for developer Richard Dansky, and it shows.<br /> <br /> (Allegedly, there were plans to do a book for Aberrant about mega-social abilities and related powers. Because this would have included cults of personality and people who would use these types of powers in very abusive ways, it was planned to carry the Black Dog label. But all of the Trinity material was moved to the Arthaus label and doing an adults only book just wasn't feasible under that set up.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T03:16:27-07:00","id":1541185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1541176#post1541176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Charnel Houses of Europe is the shining exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charnel House of Europe is a kind of fascinating thing in that it is a legitimate work of art and educational work for informing about the evils of the Holocaust.<br /> <br /> And yet it has the perhaps justified interpretation of a product that shouldn't have been made because it's still a tabletop game about the Holocaust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T03:47:20-07:00","id":1541186,"title":"","content":"I know this is heresy around here, but I think <i>Charnel Houses of Europe</i> is overrated, and puts forward some problematic viewpoints on the Holocaust. It gets portrayed as brave and artistic, but is a poorly-conceived idea which they just about got away with. It would end up leading on to some terrible books, like <i>Jerusalem by Night</i>, though that's another story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T03:59:27-07:00","id":1541187,"title":"","content":"I would argue that it is less about the Holocaust than it is about the scars it has left on the world, and I don't think you can really do a game setting like Wraith without having to talk about it at some point. <br /> <br /> I used to have a copy of a thing Richard Dansky had written (Ian Watson had posted it on the original fan site 20+ years ago) talking about the book, why he made it, some of the public flack he got, and the support he got from various people. One of them was writer Harlen Ellison, who called him in the middle of the night and told him that it was important to keep telling the story through as many mediums as possible. One of the reasons I agree with that sentiment is because I once had the experience of taking a college level US History class and literally being the only one there besides the professor who even knew what the Holocaust was. And this was back in the 1990s, when the generation that lived through it was still around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T04:03:02-07:00","id":1541188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1541186#post1541186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is heresy around here, but I think <i>Charnel Houses of Europe</i> is overrated, and puts forward some problematic viewpoints on the Holocaust. It gets portrayed as brave and artistic, but is a poorly-conceived idea which they just about got away with. It would end up leading on to some terrible books, like <i>Jerusalem by Night</i>, though that's another story.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are going to make statements like that, you really need to back them up with extensively detailed arguments and examples <b>when you are making the original assertion</b>. Otherwise, you are about one level above 4chan trolling IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T04:55:03-07:00","id":1541189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1541188#post1541188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you are going to make statements like that, you really need to back them up with extensively detailed arguments and examples <b>when you are making the original assertion</b>. Otherwise, you are about one level above 4chan trolling IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that statement wins the award for the silliest statement I have seen on this forum pretty much ever, and that's saying something.<br /> <br /> Some basic objections to <i>Charnel Houses of Europe</i>:<ul><li>The notion that the Holocaust is an event which is so particularly exception that the Ferrymen intervene in affairs. One wouldn't expect them to intervene outside of Stygian affairs, but what about the Armenian holocaust? The genocide of the Circassians?</li> <li>The portrayal of Adam Czerniakow; this is a real person, after all, and he is being portrayed as an NPC in a fairly negative light.</li> <li>...and some of the art! So, we know what Adam Czerniakow looks like, because he's a quite famous person. Look up his picture online, and you will see a well-groomed and Westernised individual (he was an engineer and politician by background). In his illustration he's very stereotypically Jewish, and this is a bit of a subtle theme throughout the book; characters we are supposed to sympathise with are portrayed as westernised, whilst less sympathetic characters are more stereotypically Jewish, which is incredibly noticeable with Czerniakow given the disparity between his appearance in the book and what he looked like in real life.</li> <li>How are we really supposed to use this book? Having a book about the Holocaust is something that could be done, but do we really need a chapter about Auschwitz? Are we supposed to be setting games here, and having fun adventures fighting the bad guys? Because whatever gaming experience you could have will invariably be in bad taste in this context.</li> </ul>I don't inherently object to creating a gaming project which touches upon historical atrocities, but the writers need to show incredible care and sensitivity, and I don't think this is always exhibited in <i>Charnel Houses of Europe</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T05:41:25-07:00","id":1541190,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry you find the idea of being asked to defend your ideas to be silly. And your objections sound fair. If you actually contacted Richard Dansky or Mark Cenczyk (who used the alias Johnathan Blacke so as not to have the book's controversial nature threaten his efforts to get his PhD in history at the time), they would probably be perfectly happy to discuss them with you.<br /> <br /> However, when you speak about a book addressing the Holocaust, created by a Jewish developer, as if it were a sly trick he managed to &quot;get away with&quot;, and then proceed to criticize another book about Jerusalem by the same developer without providing examples or context, it may appear to some as anti-Semitic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T11:54:03-07:00","id":1541205,"title":"","content":"Context matters greatly and knowing it can prevent so much trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T15:52:22-07:00","id":1541413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1541167#post1541167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there was this weird sort of schism in WWGS at the time. On the one hand, you had a bunch of people, especially developers, who were long time gamers. Some had even done some work for TSR and were open AD&amp;D fans. On the other hand, you had this group who apparently felt they were too cool for that. This seems to have involved a number of people involved with the book publishing imprint and the magazine. Especially the magazine. I have never seen another game publisher house organ go so far out of its way to avoid talking about their own company's products. And when it rebranded as Inphobia, they doubled down on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do I get the feeling that guys like Andrew Greenburg, Ron Spencer, and the Wieck Brothers were more with the former group and Justin Achilli (and his myriad successors and imitators such as Martin Ericsson and Kareem Muammar) cliqued more with the latter group?<br /> <br /> Again, I don't know for sure, but based on what others have said about them and the statements they've made and written over the years about the game, I'd believe it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 09-02-2024, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T16:17:42-07:00","id":1541416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1541413#post1541413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do I get the feeling that guys like Andrew Greenburg, Ron Spencer, and the Wieck Brothers were more with the former group</div> </div> </div> </div>Greenburg definitely. When he and Bill Bridges left White Wolf, the first thing they did was make the Fading Suns RPG, which was a pretty cool setting. The handful of interactions I had with Bill Bridges, he was always very friendly. (One of those was Fading Suns chat on AOL, similar to the ones Richard Dansky would do every month. Sadly, the only people to show up were me and writer James Estes. But both were fun to talk to, and after about 20 minutes I had run out of things to ask about Fading Suns, they were perfectly happy to talk about White Wolf stuff, particularly the Sons of Ether and Celestial Chorus tradition books.)<br /> <br /> Ethen Skemp was also very much a gamer, especially D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T17:55:47-07:00","id":1541423,"title":"","content":"OK folks, please drop this tangent of trying to pigeonhole past creators because of third and fourth-hand info. Matt Corleone, we get it: you don't like Justin. Now please stop blaming everything on him. Despite how he pops up all the time hither and yon, there were a ton of creators and many more people that made decisions that you're attributing to Justin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T18:01:13-07:00","id":1541424,"title":"","content":"Duly noted. I'll drop this side tangent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T09:41:40-07:00","id":1541456,"title":"","content":"I have to agree that Duke would have made a slightly better fit with the Tremere or even a Baali then a member of the Ventrue clan or even a Tziscme might work better for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T13:24:31-07:00","id":1542495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1541184#post1541184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a big part of Black Dog's existence is because someone at WW really, really wanted to republish Human Occupied Landfill, Dirt Merchant Games' &quot;edgy&quot; satire of early 90s rpg tropes. It and its sole sourcebook, BUTTery HOLesomeness, are the only nonWoD releases the brand ever did. And as I said, I don't consider those actual games but snarky cynical efforts at satirizing early 90s rpgs. While &quot;art&quot; is subjective, I'm not sure they qualify in the way that blurb uses the term.<br /> <br /> The other aspect of its existence probably goes back to the original Brujah clanbook from 1992. One of the templates, the Rapper, used the word &quot;fuck&quot; in its character quote, and this apparently got some pushback from a few retailers. Because Vampire and the other games billed themselves as for &quot;mature readers&quot;, I think there was always this desire to try to get into what the American movie industry would consider &quot;hard R&quot; territory and talk frankly about &quot;adult themes&quot; using &quot;adult language&quot; but also having to deal with the reality that RPGs - being primarily sold through comic book stores at the time - were essentially an &quot;all ages&quot; hobby.<br /> <br /> Plus DC had created their Vertigo imprint just a few years earlier, making comics socially acceptable for alternative hipsters who didn't want to be associated with superhero nerds, and I think WWGS was always chasing that kind of reputation in the RPG sphere.<br /> <br /> As an aside, around this same time there was a book released called Generation Ecch, a very sarcastic and cynical overview of what was being touted as Gen X cultural tropes and interests (indie films, raves, 70s nostalgia, comics, etc.). Each chapter was opened with a page by alternative comic book maker Evan Dorkin, and the comic book chapter included a panel pointing out that most &quot;mature/adult&quot; comics just ended up being an excuse to swear a lot and draw naked breasts. And if you are familiar with most of the Black Dog label books, you know exactly why I brought that up.<br /> <br /> The initial wave was four books, one for each line. (God only knows what sort of book they'd have tried for Changeling if that line hasn't just been starting.) And I don't think any of them sold as well as was hoped.<br /> <br /> I've never fully read the entire Giovoni Chronicles, so I can't really say if they needed to be Black Dog or not. Honestly, I think insisting that the three follow up volumes also carry the label is what even kept the BD brand alive for the next few years.<br /> <br /> Freak Legion may as well be the poster child for what I mentioned earlier. It is almost entirely juvenile shock value for shock value's sake.<br /> <br /> Destiny's Price was a good idea, as a guide to inner city street life, the underground club scene, and gutterpunk culture is the sort of thing that would be useful for all of the WoD game lines. Unfortunately, this book is just sort of there. It never really got into the sort of detail about sex, drugs, and violence that would really justify this having the BD label. It feels like this was just going to be a regular book on the release schedule, got picked to be part of this project, and so the art department threw in a few pictures of S&amp;M strippers with bare breasts. (It wasn't really helped that shortly after it was released, films such as Trainspotting and Kids came out, making this instantly feel a little sanitized and dated.)<br /> <br /> Wraith's Spectres book was probably the one that came closest to deserving the Black Dog brand. Wraith was already a somewhat dark game that rewarded a type of roleplaying based on delving into what made your character tick and what baggage they carried around. With Spectres, you had that compounded by a massive amount of nihilism that I think is best left to players with a certain level of emotional maturity.<br /> <br /> Montreal by Night always felt like it was using the BD label as a marketing gimmick. It really didn't need it, but &quot;Oooooh, it's a Sabbat city, come look at how eeeeeevil and wicked they are!&quot; Plus some gratuitous human toilets.<br /> <br /> Clanbook Baali really has no good reason to exist. While half of the book does have some interesting ideas about prehistoric elder gods, it also wastes time with juvenile shock material (including really gross opening fiction that feels like it was written to appeal to the National Association of Marlan Brando Look-Alikes).<br /> <br /> The Cainite Heresy probably didn't really need the label but got it mainly because of the focus on religious sects and its reexaminations of the Path of Evil Revelations. The fact that it was written by two skilled authors, Ken Hite and R Sean Borgstrom, certainly helped elevate its quality.<br /> <br /> Finally, Charnel Houses of Europe. I think this is the only book that ever really lived up to the label's potential. It is a serious look at a serious subject, and endeavors to use roleplaying games as a teaching tool to help educate people about the Holocaust. It was a deeply personal project for developer Richard Dansky, and it shows.<br /> <br /> (Allegedly, there were plans to do a book for Aberrant about mega-social abilities and related powers. Because this would have included cults of personality and people who would use these types of powers in very abusive ways, it was planned to carry the Black Dog label. But all of the Trinity material was moved to the Arthaus label and doing an adults only book just wasn't feasible under that set up.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for the thread necromancy, but I was thinking about this old post and it got me thinking about Black Dog in general.<br /> <br /> I'd say Hunter Book: Wayward was a good final note for the Black Dog label, coming out in either 2001 or early 2002, years after the previous Black Dog releases, IIRC. Supposedly the Black Dog label was about to be phased out entirely but was brought out one last time for the Wayward book due to how the book handles subjects like psychopathy, murder, and ordinary humans who snap.<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely curious what Changeling's Black Dog book was going to be, if any such thing was planned at all, and I know for a fact that Ghouls: Fatal Addiction was initially planned to be a Black Dog release but Rob Hatch made a last-second decision to have it be a general VTM release since it was a flagship for the Year of the Ally promotion and he wanted to get home early that night to watch WCW Monday Nitro.<br /> <br /> I was also wondering about some books that could've been Black Dog books but weren't.<br /> <br /> Ghouls Fatal Addiction is the big one, and so was the original Clanbook Tzimisce (to the point it sometimes gets put on lists of the Black Dog releases)<br /> <br /> I also think the infamous Earthbound book for Demon: The Fallen could've been a contender for the label given how it handled religious subject matter, but by then, Black Dog was a relic being phased out","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 09-21-2024, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T15:09:06-07:00","id":1542498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542495#post1542495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also think the infamous Earthbound book for Demon: The Fallen could've been a contender for the label given how it handled religious subject matter, but by then, Black Dog was a relic being phased out</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. IIRC Earthbound still has a very shallow take on religion. Overall DtF\u2019s weak point was its take on religions outside Christianity, and Earthbound is basically pop culture Cults.<br /> <br /> Given the Black Dog treatment, I think it would devolve into Lovecraft Lectures on Religion all the way instead of gaining any quality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T20:26:43-07:00","id":1542501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542498#post1542498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know. IIRC Earthbound still has a very shallow take on religion. Overall DtF\u2019s weak point was its take on religions outside Christianity, and Earthbound is basically pop culture Cults.<br /> <br /> Given the Black Dog treatment, I think it would devolve into Lovecraft Lectures on Religion all the way instead of gaining any quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.<br /> <br /> Tbh, Demon in general felt like an edgier premise than any other White Wolf game up to that point (with the possible exception of Wraith) but it wasn't quite that edgy in its execution.<br /> <br /> I still wonder what Black Dog books for Changeling would've looked like. Or Werewolf: The Wild West.<br /> <br /> Given the time and place, I assume KOTE's Black Dog book would've been in the ballpark of &quot;Men Behind The Sun meets old-school ero-guro hentai&quot; and that's a whole can of worms best left unopened.<br /> <br /> IIRC, didn't Mage: The Sorcerer's Crusade get a Black Dog book? IIRC, it was Infernalism: The Path of Screams, though I'm not as familiar with that line and it may have been another case similar to Clanbook: Tzimisce or Ghouls: Fatal Addiction where it &quot;feels&quot; like a Black Dog book and will occasionally get misreported as such in retrospect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T22:20:57-07:00","id":1542504,"title":"","content":"The actual splat with which PCs can really go all the way to being truly, unspeakably evil, and be rewarded by the mechanics instead of punished, as strange as it seems, is Changeling. A game most edgelords pay no attention to. In fact it has an excess of \u201cNightmare Flavors\u201d, as dev after dev that worked in the line didn\u2019t grasp how dark it could be already and invented a new EVIL subsplat.<br /> <br /> But from Changeling core alone you can already have things like a child-eating serial-killer who makes extra money every week kidnapping teenagers for parties where they\u2019ll be drugged and raped. And the only reason you\u2019re not an upstanding member of your community is that the Body-Snatcher Invaders who make up for most of nobility find you uncouth at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T22:42:10-07:00","id":1542505,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how the Earthbound could be used to discuss non-Christian religion given they're apocalyptic world destroying one dimensionally evil monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T00:38:54-07:00","id":1542508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542501#post1542501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still wonder what Black Dog books for Changeling would've looked like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly it's not too hard to imagine that Book of Houses 2, the one about the Unseelie Houses, could have easily ended up being a Black Dog book if they had focused more on thd monstrous inhumanity of the Unseelie Houses and the ways in which they ravish Glamor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T11:34:48-07:00","id":1542512,"title":"","content":"I dunno, Black Dog always felt really....unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I think the only one that needed the label was Ghouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T16:15:07-07:00","id":1542517,"title":"","content":"This is something of a tangent perhaps but I do want to say a couple words in Demon\u2019s honor, at least in the sense that there was some potential there that could have been nurtured at one point and time. <br /> <br /> Obviously it\u2019s a matter of taste but having Demon deal with cults that feel like they could have been shaken out of the Exorcist III or a Lovecraft story isn\u2019t inherently a bad thing. That pulpy occultism and Satanism still has traction in the vocabulary of horror that WoD has always tapped into and I definitely think something could have been developed to bring out something along those lines.<br /> <br /> Of course there would still be room for a metatextual discussion about the significance and usefulness of the sub-genre.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know, I feel like I haven\u2019t fully fleshed this out but I hope that this makes sense:<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a tendency (which I certainly participate in fwiw) in parts of ttrpg spaces to look at the inherited trappings of the genre and put them under the microscope. A classic example is the standard faux-Satanic cult of evil of your run of the mill D&amp;D or Call of Cthulhu scenario. These get criticized, correctly, for portraying a more or less entirely phantasmagorical image which does not resemble what most cults actually look like. So there\u2019s a movement to replace these groups with more realistic alternatives (or do without them entirely).<br /> <br /> However there\u2019s another tendency, an impulse, to maintain the old tradition, and it\u2019s not just held by beer-and-pretzels gamers who don\u2019t particularly want to think about it. There\u2019s another tendency which points out that, even if time has rendered some of these ideas somewhat comic and that they\u2019re often used lazily, they still do have a kernel of artistic potence which has the capacity to capture an audience. This tendency argues that it\u2019s worthwhile to keep these elements, around even if they are basically anachronistic, because under the layers of cheap imitation there\u2019s something solid.<br /> <br /> I think both ends of this spectrum have good points abt the implicit politics, storytelling potency, etc. of these sorts of things. I for one try to carry out a sort of dialectic between the two - maintaining what\u2019s of value from the old pulp material but under the influence of modern times. <br /> <br /> I hope this wasn\u2019t too tangential or meandering but the direction of the conversation brought this to mind for me and I figured I\u2019d share my two cents. Hope y\u2019all are having a good one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T19:05:15-07:00","id":1542519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542517#post1542517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However there\u2019s another tendency, an impulse, to maintain the old tradition, and it\u2019s not just held by beer-and-pretzels gamers who don\u2019t particularly want to think about it. There\u2019s another tendency which points out that, even if time has rendered some of these ideas somewhat comic and that they\u2019re often used lazily, they still do have a kernel of artistic potence which has the capacity to capture an audience. This tendency argues that it\u2019s worthwhile to keep these elements, around even if they are basically anachronistic, because under the layers of cheap imitation there\u2019s something solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a funny essay I wish I still had that I wrote in college that stated that Cthulhu cults were actually satire so clever that no one realized it. It was that they were Lovecraft poking fun at Christian eschatology rather than making generically evil cults.<br /> <br /> Cthulhu is, after all:<br /> <br /> * A dead god who will rise again<br /> * A god who will bring the end of the world<br /> * A god who is worshiped by all races and social classes<br /> * A god whose followers want to bring about the end of the world<br /> * A god who will smite the unbeliever and reward the faithful<br /> <br /> Which is to say that doomsday end of the world cults are not necessarily as unrealistic as we may think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T21:47:23-07:00","id":1542521,"title":"","content":"So this is the list of Black Dog titles<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b><br /> Giovanni Chronicles <br /> Montreal By Night<br /> Eternal Hearts<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</b><br /> Freak Legion<br /> <br /> <b>Mage: The Ascension</b><br /> Destiny's Price<br /> Dead Magic<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: The Dark Ages</b><br /> Clanbook Baali<br /> Cainite Heresy<br /> <br /> <b>Wraith: The Oblivion</b><br /> Dark Reflections: Spectres<br /> Charnel Houses of Europe: The Shoah<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter: The Reckoning</b><br /> Hunter Book: Wayward<br /> <br /> <b>Not Black Dog, but tends to get misremembered as such</b><br /> Clanbook: Tzimisce<br /> Clanbook: Giovanni<br /> Infernalism: The Path of Screams<br /> Chronicles of the Black Labyrinth<br /> Ghouls: Fatal Addiction<br /> <br /> I do find it interesting that Dead Magic was the penultimate Black Dog book and was released so long after almost all the others. The Wayward book was for a line that didn't exist in 1994-1998 when the main cluster of Black Dog books came out, and IIRC, the book even mentions in its foreword that it was done as a send-off to the Black Dog label and because of the content involved when it comes to roleplaying a Wayward warranted the Black Dog label.<br /> <br /> Charnel Houses of Europe was a personal pet project for Richard Dansky,<br /> <br /> Dead Magic came out in 2000, during the Revised years, when Black Dog was seen as a relic. I don't own Dead Magic, so maybe there's something I'm missing as to why it warranted a Black Dog release but wasn't it just about the magic traditions of ancient cultures?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T22:02:51-07:00","id":1542522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542517#post1542517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something of a tangent perhaps but I do want to say a couple words in Demon\u2019s honor, at least in the sense that there was some potential there that could have been nurtured at one point and time.</div> </div> </div> </div>My comment was in the specific context of Earthbound being made a Black Dog book, and how it would turn out if the reason were \u201creligious commentary\u201d.<br /> <br /> Let me be clear, first, that Demon is my favorite WoD game, period. It is a good commentary on Christianity and the things people do in its name, and it is overall an interesting premise with a lot of potential.<br /> <br /> And cults aren\u2019t just a powerful genre tradition. They\u2019re a phenomenon that actually does exist. If anything, the difference is that many (but not all) of them are actually Christian in their core, but personality cults are out there in the real world, making real victims, be it by controlling the lives of members, sucking their livelihoods for money, breaking families and social support of their victims, and even leading people to mass suicides or terrorism.<br /> <br /> Demon had a problem with its representation of other religions, not with its representation of the phenomenon of personality cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T23:14:07-07:00","id":1542524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542522#post1542522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demon had a problem with its representation of other religions, not with its representation of the phenomenon of personality cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon's problem is basically the problem of In Nomine.<br /> <br /> How does one deal with a game that requires one's premise for one religion to be objectively true?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T14:27:33-07:00","id":1542581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542524#post1542524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demon's problem is basically the problem of In Nomine.<br /> <br /> How does one deal with a game that requires one's premise for one religion to be objectively true?</div> </div> </div> </div>My current solution, built in another thread here, is that it is objectively true in <i><b>a version</b></i> of the WoD, but not necessarily the version they're released.<br /> <br /> Add multiversal shenanigans and they may have applicable knowledge even if the origin of this knowledge is uncertain. For example, a Bastion may be something that exists in its own shard of reality in such a way that it can be accessed from a given place even if it is another version of that place than the one where it waas created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T16:02:33-07:00","id":1542589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542521#post1542521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dead Magic came out in 2000, during the Revised years, when Black Dog was seen as a relic. I don't own Dead Magic, so maybe there's something I'm missing as to why it warranted a Black Dog release but wasn't it just about the magic traditions of ancient cultures?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had no idea <i>Dead Magic</i> was a Black Dog release. Admittedly, it's been a while since I cracked the book open and read it. But it never struck me as being a particularly &quot;adult&quot; text. Not unless I'm forgetting some pretty glaring points, like explicit art or subject matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T16:29:26-07:00","id":1542590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542581#post1542581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My current solution, built in another thread here, is that it is objectively true in <i><b>a version</b></i> of the WoD, but not necessarily the version they're released.<br /> <br /> Add multiversal shenanigans and they may have applicable knowledge even if the origin of this knowledge is uncertain. For example, a Bastion may be something that exists in its own shard of reality in such a way that it can be accessed from a given place even if it is another version of that place than the one where it waas created.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a messier solution but one that amused me.<br /> <br /> Demons absolutely believe their version to be true and have plenty of evidence.<br /> <br /> And then they run into werewolves or Kuei Jin who ALSO have contradictory evidence their versions are true.<br /> <br /> And there's absolutely no explanation for how all of them fit together.<br /> <br /> Except from mages...and fuck those guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-25-2024, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T16:54:24-07:00","id":1542595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542590#post1542590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a messier solution but one that amused me.<br /> <br /> Demons absolutely believe their version to be true and have plenty of evidence.<br /> <br /> And then they run into werewolves or Kuei Jin wo ALSO have contradictory evidence their versions are true.<br /> <br /> And there's absolutely no explanation for how all of them fit together.<br /> <br /> Except from mages...and fuck those guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. Mages probably have things closest to &quot;correct&quot;, by virtue of their whole &quot;Consensual Reality&quot; thing allowing for everyone else's worldview to work, within its context.<br /> <br /> But no one - not even Mages - really like to accept that answer, if they're even aware of it. Because that would mean surrendering their subjective view of reality as being one among many valid &quot;Paradigms&quot; that all, simultaneously, work. The splats - even individual Mages - prefer to see their own worldview as objectively correct, and everyone else just a weird edge case or mystery not worth worrying about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T21:40:59-07:00","id":1542605,"title":"","content":"There really isn't any reason for Dead Magic to have the BD label that I can remember. (Dead Magic 2 was IIRC supposed to carry the Year of the Damned logo but ended up not.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T22:09:10-07:00","id":1542607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542605#post1542605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There really isn't any reason for Dead Magic to have the BD label that I can remember. (Dead Magic 2 was IIRC supposed to carry the Year of the Damned logo but ended up not.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I had a theory about why Dead Magic got the BD release and tbh, this is just wild speculation on my part and I'm probably wrong about it and I'd genuinely appreciate it if someone more in the know could help clarify it<br /> <br /> I think the fact that it deals with human sacrifice is what got it the label specifically but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> As for why that was suddenly a hot-button issue given how similar themes appeared in material regarding groups like the Sabbat, the Baali, infernalists, or the Wyrmish factions, I have no idea.<br /> <br /> At first I was wondering if it was because of Columbine briefly revitalizing the Satanic Panic on a national level to an extent but I don't think that was the reason as more books would've been slapped with that label and the only White Wolf game that got any flack at all after the Columbine tragedy was Vampire, and that was a very minor controversy at best that would've been completely forgotten about had it not been for The Escapist website writing its own rebuttal to that controversy.<br /> <br /> So I'm pretty sure it wasn't that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 09-25-2024, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T00:24:04-07:00","id":1542617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542595#post1542595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, absolutely. Mages probably have things closest to &quot;correct&quot;, by virtue of their whole &quot;Consensual Reality&quot; thing allowing for everyone else's worldview to work, within its context.<br /> <br /> But no one - not even Mages - really like to accept that answer, if they're even aware of it. Because that would mean surrendering their subjective view of reality as being one among many valid &quot;Paradigms&quot; that all, simultaneously, work. The splats - even individual Mages - prefer to see their own worldview as objectively correct, and everyone else just a weird edge case or mystery not worth worrying about.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf mentioned the idea of multiple Worlds of Darknesses existing with the importance of each splat rearranging based on which one you were playing.<br /> <br /> I considered the possibility as an actual in-universe thing and more Mage: The Awakening.<br /> <br /> Multiple spheres and universes intersecting.<br /> <br /> So like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> suggested.<br /> <br /> But I SLIGHTLY prefer the mystery, &quot;Okay, I <i>know</i> God, what the fuck is going on? Who is this Gaia person?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-25-2024, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T08:11:23-07:00","id":1542631,"title":"","content":"Someone, and I wish I could remember who (I want to say Ethan Skemp or Bruce Baugh, but Geoff Grabowski is another likely culprit), explained their take as that while all off these games nominally share the same setting, each has its own distinct cosmology, and which one is true depends on which game you are actually playing. And for the most part, if you are playing, say, Vampire, then Werewolf's non-humancentric animism or Mage's gnostic consensual reality don't really matter when it comes to what Kindred are doing in their everynight unlives. Similarly, Vampire's dark Christian\u00b9 cosmology doesn't really matter when playing those other games (and in some cases may not even matter when playing Vampire if you aren't doing anything involving the Final Nights or Noddism). <br /> It only really becomes an issue when doing crossovers. Werewolf and Mage, for example, are harder to do because they have almost totally opposite positions on the importance of humanity and their place in the cosmology. Vampire and Demon, on the other hand, is probably easier. (In hindsight, I really wish they'd done a dedicated crossover guide for each pair of game lines - Vampire + Werewolf, Vampire + Mage, etc. - that went over all the reasons the two groups might interact and what issues the Storyteller would have to work out beforehand.) <br /> <br /> \u00b9 &quot;Dark Christian&quot; was a phrase Bruce Baugh came up with IIRC. The general idea is that God exists and He is a very harsh and judgmental God, and while the potential for redemption/salvation exists, it is a long and difficult road to travel. Also, demons are real, and if you ever actually met an angel, it would be incredibly terrifying. In many ways, it is influenced by what you see in certain Gothic fiction, some 80s and 90s movies involving angels and demons, and Jack Chick tracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T13:44:28-07:00","id":1542639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542631#post1542631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u00b9 &quot;Dark Christian&quot; was a phrase Bruce Baugh came up with IIRC. The general idea is that God exists and He is a very harsh and judgmental God, and while the potential for redemption/salvation exists, it is a long and difficult road to travel. Also, demons are real, and if you ever actually met an angel, it would be incredibly terrifying. In many ways, it is influenced by what you see in certain Gothic fiction, some 80s and 90s movies involving angels and demons, and Jack Chick tracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Southerner in the Bible Belt in the Nineties, I feel V:TM very neatly tapped into the counterculture of the time.<br /> <br /> &quot;What if God was real...but a bastard?&quot;<br /> <br /> 1st Edition basically has this as a central thesis. &quot;You are damned through no fault of your own and any possibility of escaping damnation requires a convoluted set of rules and actions [golconda] that may be impossible.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T16:43:34-07:00","id":1542651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542639#post1542639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a Southerner in the Bible Belt in the Nineties, I feel V:TM very neatly tapped into the counterculture of the time.<br /> <br /> &quot;What if God was real...but a bastard?&quot;<br /> <br /> 1st Edition basically has this as a central thesis. &quot;You are damned through no fault of your own and any possibility of escaping damnation requires a convoluted set of rules and actions [golconda] that may be impossible.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, V1 also made Golconda seemingly much easier to obtain than it would become in later editions. The comic running through the length of the book had the newly Embraced deuteragonist seemingly cure his vampirism simply by killing his Sire. So, Golconda was positioned as a mysterious, but nonetheless &quot;doable&quot;, goal to achieve in-game. It's only later that writers started really hammering on the grimdark idea that not only is Golconda nigh impossible, it may not even be desirable.<br /> <br /> But back on track, yes, Vampire: The Masquerade seemed built on the idea of rebellion against the Christian power structures of America during the time of its designers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T17:01:11-07:00","id":1542652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542651#post1542651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Granted, V1 also made Golconda seemingly much easier to obtain than it would become in later editions. The comic running through the length of the book had the newly Embraced deuteragonist seemingly cure his vampirism simply by killing his Sire. So, Golconda was positioned as a mysterious, but nonetheless &quot;doable&quot;, goal to achieve in-game. It's only later that writers started really hammering on the grimdark idea that not only is Golconda nigh impossible, it may not even be desirable.<br /> <br /> But back on track, yes, Vampire: The Masquerade seemed built on the idea of rebellion against the Christian power structures of America during the time of its designers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which I actually feel is kind of central.<br /> <br /> It also explains some of the issue as atheist, arreligious, or simply uncaring players for that theme got annoyed that there was so much &quot;inherited guilt/original sin&quot; hanging over being a cool undead monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T19:03:18-07:00","id":1542655,"title":"","content":"If you want a good example of the sort of mindset and cultural landscape that produced first edition Vampire, I recommend checking out Queensr\u00ffche's 1988 concept album/rock opera <i>Operation: Mindcrime</i>. (You can probably find the entire album as well as the Livecrime concert version on YouTube.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T20:11:29-07:00","id":1542659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542590#post1542590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a messier solution but one that amused me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my solution to contradictions between splats is simpler and, well, maybe messier, maybe not.<br /> <br /> They simply don\u2019t live in the same reality.<br /> <br /> When I ST a game, one splat is \u201cthe main\u201d, and reality is built around them. The objective truth, if at all relevant, is theirs or related to them. All the others, while mechanically working as per their own rules for most of it (because that\u2019s simpler to my head), are objectively wrong and their lore is just legend.<br /> <br /> No, my previous \u201csolution\u201d was meant for the idea of Christianity as objectively true against all other religions, current or ancient.<br /> <br /> In my games, gods exist. And they\u2019re gods. Trying to define which religion is truer is immaterial, they\u2019re gods for all intents and purposes and can prove, if not their stories, their power and place in Creation. Gods aren\u2019t Angels/Demons in disguise. They aren\u2019t just stories. They\u2019re rare to interfere in anything, but when they do, they\u2019re simply more. And they exist simultaneously in infinite versions of reality.<br /> <br /> Oh, and for whatever it\u2019s worth, my take pertains more to how I picture things or take decisions if and when needed. From an in-character perspective and even for my players, the answer is pretty much unknowable unless they invest A LOT into learning it.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear on my context, living in the biggest Catholic country in the world, I know very well how it is to be surrounded by a deeply Christian society, where even being a minority, the heavily religious are disproportionately powerful and loud, be them traditional Catholics or the growing Evangelical almost-not-a-minority-anymore.<br /> <br /> But this is also the country of Candombl\u00e9 and Umbanda, of persecution to the last followers of native religions, and heavy persecution against \u201cNew Age\u201d, which usually means neo-pagan beliefs. And I\u2019m a neo-pagan myself. I can\u2019t think about the matter surrounding Demon and Vampire only in terms of Christianity being true or not, I have to consider the space given to other beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T21:54:47-07:00","id":1542853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542659#post1542659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, my solution to contradictions between splats is simpler and, well, maybe messier, maybe not.<br /> <br /> They simply don\u2019t live in the same reality.<br /> <br /> When I ST a game, one splat is \u201cthe main\u201d, and reality is built around them. The objective truth, if at all relevant, is theirs or related to them. All the others, while mechanically working as per their own rules for most of it (because that\u2019s simpler to my head), are objectively wrong and their lore is just legend.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much how I do it as well. When I'm running vampire, mages are just reality-cancer. They are powerful, but reality's immune system is always trying to purge them. All their beliefs about themselves is just a nonsense attempt to make themselves more than they are. But when I'm running Mage, everything Mages believe about themselves is real, and vampires are just bygones that have lasted a bit longer than most because of a combination of their popularity in fiction and by draining humans of quintessence. If I'm running werewolf, vampires are just an odd type of fomori and mages are just humans that have connected with some powerful spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T23:01:18-07:00","id":1542854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542853#post1542853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's pretty much how I do it as well. When I'm running vampire, mages are just reality-cancer. They are powerful, but reality's immune system is always trying to purge them. All their beliefs about themselves is just a nonsense attempt to make themselves more than they are. But when I'm running Mage, everything Mages believe about themselves is real, and vampires are just bygones that have lasted a bit longer than most because of a combination of their popularity in fiction and by draining humans of quintessence. If I'm running werewolf, vampires are just an odd type of fomori and mages are just humans that have connected with some powerful spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my mage games, I had something that was VERY DEVASTATING to mage believers that they all go instantly into denial over.<br /> <br /> &quot;Is it really likely that reality is consensual or is it MORE likely that the universe is just solid and real but can be altered by AWAKENED belief's but Awakened will probably never be more than a tiny minority of people, possibly only those with significant avatars?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T00:35:28-07:00","id":1542858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542854#post1542854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my mage games, I had something that was VERY DEVASTATING to mage believers that they all go instantly into denial over.<br /> <br /> &quot;Is it really likely that reality is consensual or is it MORE likely that the universe is just solid and real but can be altered by AWAKENED belief's but Awakened will probably never be more than a tiny minority of people, possibly only those with significant avatars?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I ended up having to do something similar, just to save myself headaches as a GM and to head off potential arguments at the table. Reality is what it is, but Awakening is coming to understand that there is an underlying Tapestry that maintains it, and Sphere Magic allows you to tweak the Tapestry to manipulate Reality. And avatars are the shattered fragments of the beings that used to maintain the Tapestry prior to whatever pre-historic event broke the world into its current state rather than something people are born with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T02:35:58-07:00","id":1542860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542858#post1542858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I ended up having to do something similar, just to save myself headaches as a GM and to head off potential arguments at the table. Reality is what it is, but Awakening is coming to understand that there is an underlying Tapestry that maintains it, and Sphere Magic allows you to tweak the Tapestry to manipulate Reality. And avatars are the shattered fragments of the beings that used to maintain the Tapestry prior to whatever pre-historic event broke the world into its current state rather than something people are born with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Occams' Razor solution which would probably be the most likely &quot;correct&quot; solution.<br /> <br /> But it means that the entire Ascension War is over a misunderstanding of mages wanting to believe they're God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T06:12:33-07:00","id":1542865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542860#post1542860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the Occams' Razor solution which would probably be the most likely &quot;correct&quot; solution.<br /> <br /> But it means that the entire Ascension War is over a misunderstanding of mages wanting to believe they're God.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem with that postulate is that it cannot explain either reality zones or the apparition and variations of paradox across history. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T07:16:36-07:00","id":1542867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542865#post1542865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The problem with that postulate is that it cannot explain either reality zones or the apparition and variations of paradox across history.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably, it means the problem is not with reality but how magic works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T07:38:42-07:00","id":1542868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542867#post1542867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arguably, it means the problem is not with reality but how magic works.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's inherently the same. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T09:48:21-07:00","id":1542870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542868#post1542868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's inherently the same.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And yes, that is why mage have killed each other for a thousand years over nothing in this premise.<br /> <br /> &quot;Healing Magic is altered by the fact people believe in faith healing there!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Egads, man! That means that faith healing would work for everyone if we just BELIEVE hard enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sir, that's not...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;KILL ALL THE SCIENTISTS, DANIEL!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T11:11:34-07:00","id":1542872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542865#post1542865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with that postulate is that it cannot explain either reality zones or the apparition and variations of paradox across history.</div> </div> </div> </div>The postulate that is being put forward here is that there's a baseline reality here and now that doesn't have to be explained as existing because people believe it exists; it exists independently of whatever the human Consensus says. There's nothing saying that it has to be the same <i>there </i>as it is <i>here, </i>or that it will be the same in the future as it is in the present or was in the past; the only thing it says is that humans aren't the be-all and end-all determinors of what reality is. <br /> <br /> And yes, this <i>is</i> compatible with &quot;the Ascension War only exists because mages have God complexes&quot;. That's the inherent horror of Mage, after all: people with godlike power and human foibles. <br /> <br /> (Now let me go back and read this thread to see how a Vampire topic ended up mutating into a discussion of Mage philosophy. Should be interesting.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T22:41:27-07:00","id":1542894,"title":"","content":"It would be funny if all mages turned out to be were viruses. This group of mages the flu, that group measles, the other covid. All that hubris, and reality just considers them all diseases its immune system constantly fights off. What would that make technocrats? Another virus, or a vaccine, a virus that the immune system has suborned for its own protection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T10:11:31-07:00","id":1542916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542894#post1542894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be funny if all mages turned out to be were viruses. This group of mages the flu, that group measles, the other covid. All that hubris, and reality just considers them all diseases its immune system constantly fights off. What would that make technocrats? Another virus, or a vaccine, a virus that the immune system has suborned for its own protection?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you consider the ages past as the default state of reality, so things wondrous and magical were more common, then the Technocrats would be malignant cancer in this analogy. Nephandus would be a type of necrosis, and Marauders would be mutations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T11:17:39-07:00","id":1542919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542916#post1542916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you consider the ages past as the default state of reality, so things wondrous and magical were more common, then the Technocrats would be malignant cancer in this analogy. Nephandus would be a type of necrosis, and Marauders would be mutations.</div> </div> </div> </div>A curious analogy, since mutations frequently lead to malignant cancer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T12:39:06-07:00","id":1542922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542919#post1542919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A curious analogy, since mutations frequently lead to malignant cancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I originally was going to write &quot;genetic aberrations&quot; but I didn't want it to be misconstrued as some kind of ableism. Mutations felt broad and neutral enough.<br /> <br /> Linguistics aside, Marauders have a lot of potential to be both the most dangerous things in existence and the most benign things depending on the individual. Some are definitely in the, if not put down in some way, will lead to the warping and destruction of reality, while others are, &quot;everything in the area I'm in smells like purple.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","v