/forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542872#post1542872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The postulate that is being put forward here is that there's a baseline reality here and now that doesn't have to be explained as existing because people believe it exists; it exists independently of whatever the human Consensus says. There's nothing saying that it has to be the same <i>there </i>as it is <i>here, </i>or that it will be the same in the future as it is in the present or was in the past; the only thing it says is that humans aren't the be-all and end-all determinors of what reality is.<br /> <br /> And yes, this <i>is</i> compatible with &quot;the Ascension War only exists because mages have God complexes&quot;. That's the inherent horror of Mage, after all: people with godlike power and human foibles.<br /> <br /> (Now let me go back and read this thread to see how a Vampire topic ended up mutating into a discussion of Mage philosophy. Should be interesting.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The thing is human belief is the factor that systematically precedes tgese changes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T07:26:06-07:00","id":1542951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542949#post1542949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is human belief is the factor that systematically precedes tgese changes</div> </div> </div> </div>And what if...Awakening was the difference.<br /> <br /> And human belief might affect Awakened magic results but has no tangible effects on reality as a whole beyond but magic resutls.<br /> <br /> People believe in faith healing, easier to do for Awakening.<br /> .<br /> But all normal people die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T09:36:58-07:00","id":1542954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542872#post1542872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...humans aren't the be-all and end-all determinors of what reality is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also kind of a non-starter, purely academic, argument in the same vein as &quot;what existed before the Big Bang?&quot;. It is, for all intents and purposes, devoid of all practical purpose. The Tapestry exists and so do non-human entities; however, it's human collective consciousness that defines the former, and determines the capability of the latter to interact with and influence the Tapestry.<br /> <br /> I think what's lost in this tangential discussion is Sleepers have Avatars, too. It's through the unconscious influence of sleeping Avatars that consensus -- local, regional, or global, historic or contemporary -- forms. That may be the full extent of a sleeping Avatar's influence upon reality and consensus, but that influence still exists.<br /> <br /> There are two examples that really present the case, than which we really needn't look further: bygones, and the panoply of cthonic entities that inhabit the Deep Umbra. The plight of bygones speaks for itself, but that the Umbrood inhabiting the Deep Umbra are largely indefinite, indifferent, and by most accounts insapient <i>until impinged upon by human presence</i> speaks to the full extent of human influence on the Tapestry.<br /> <br /> The very fact we can question if these entities even exist in any form other than as Quintessence until observed by Awakened or Sleepers, is in itself the evidence of the point. We can't get around that even the most skeptical and empiricist Awakened mage and their cohort still carries implicit bias and some degree of expectation based on past experience out there, and it's inherently unknowable if, say, the Flying Spaghetti Monster really was out there all along just waiting to be discovered, or if the Flying Spaghetti Monster spontaneously manifested out of Quintessence in response to someone making a dumb quip that made its way through the voidship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T10:22:13-07:00","id":1542959,"title":"","content":"DISREGARD HUMAN BELIEF<br /> [advicemokole.png]<br /> WE SHAPED THEM OUT OF BASAL PRIMATES, REMEMBER?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T10:34:06-07:00","id":1542963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542951#post1542951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what if...Awakening was the difference.<br /> <br /> And human belief might affect Awakened magic results but has no tangible effects on reality as a whole beyond but magic resutls.<br /> <br /> People believe in faith healing, easier to do for Awakening.<br /> .<br /> But all normal people die.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, for a start, you can do that for your table. Howether, that would not be what MtAs states and shows.<br /> <br /> While we mostly see the impact of the consensus on mages, we have across the books (scarcely, because clearly the authors were not really committed to that part of the game metaphysics) direct evidence of the consensus shaping reality without awakened intervention.<br /> <br /> For a start, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a> mentionned, bygones are only running scarves due to the lack of belief. It's states multiple times and repeatedly in the bygone bestiary.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, nations were erased from consensual reality toward the umbra thanks to belief that they don't exist. This is clearly stated through dark age mage, Victorian mage and both void engineers convention books.<br /> <br /> We also have multiple what if scenarios described in books where variance in domination in the ascension war shaped reality for everyone. Notably one possible world where the sons of ether became the dominant paradigm of the technocracy. And our science don't work for sleepers, only dynamic science can be produced.<br /> <br /> Same for another where future traditions won and convinced humanity of their own magical potential, making a world where every sleepers has one level 1 or 2 magical effect as an inherent capability.<br /> <br /> So in MtA, in a reality zone shaped by the belief in faith healing, normal people can do it too, as long as they met the required criteria of faith. Just as we require to meet the criterias of medicine.<br /> <br /> This also goes back in time. Dark age Mage specifically and sorcerer's crusade to a lesser extent precise that sleepers can't make modern technology at all, and that superstition shapes their existence, the exemple given of curses being a thing even a sleeper can levy on others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course I'm not in any way telling you how to run your game or your homeruling. But I sometime wonder, when listening to people talking about the topic on this forum, if they don't forget that consensus is not just about mages and that, ironically, is not a belief.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: while I'm thinking of it, the idea that consensus only limits mages also imply that the baseline reality is a mystical one, as the world's past is one rightfully called the high mythic age. It would hardly be our own science based one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T13:31:12-07:00","id":1542977,"title":"","content":"IDK how the thread went into crossover, but I have some ideas I wanted to share:<br /> <br /> *The &quot;Consensus shapes Reality&quot; angle it's, of course, going to be contentious. However, I don't think it's as central to mages as one would think. Perhaps more than that, what Mage put's into question it's how &quot;normal&quot; it's normal people. The whole concept of Awakened lays on the ground of humans having the &quot;potential&quot; to Awaken. More than to reality being inherently subjective, Mage talks about how &quot;humanity can change the world&quot;<br /> <br /> The Consensus it's, basically, the collective Will of sleeping humanity shaping the world. However, this doesn't mean that there was no world prior to humanity, that humanity can shape reality doesn't mean that there's no objective reality. And the extent and nature of this shaping it's debatable.<br /> <br /> For instance, Bygones are chased off-world by Unbelief.<br /> <br /> It could be that Humanity rejection acts as a sort of magical attack, some couldn't resist. But otherwise they could exist w/o our belief<br /> <br /> Let's note that Enlightenment Era (overhyped) pradigm shift wasn't the only thing that hapened.<br /> Reality itself was becoming more solid causing a diminishment of the amounts of Quintessence that was already felt by Tremere on the DA (making it harder to be a thaumnivore).<br /> On crossover you could add stuff like Banality rising as Fae left for Arcadia ...<br /> <br /> The world became more hostile in several ways, that include a change of belief systems, but arguably goes beyond that.<br /> <br /> But<i> in any case</i> it's undeniable that belief it's powerful. In fact, on WoD Faith CAN heal. Even in Vampire, if I remember correctly, it's one of the things Faith can do. It's just that you need a lot of it <hr /><br /> *Now, from the perspective of Vampire: Vampire never tells you that the curse it's the only source of magic. On the contrary, it's evident that humans have inherent potential for mystical power. Faith it's dangerous. Sorcerers exist. A normal person you killed could transform into a ghost and pursue you with their ghost magic. And whatever it's going on in the Ebony Kingdom ... The idea that humanity has inherent supernatural potential it's not something that should be too shocking to the Occult saavy vampire<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the Vampire sees humans as victims. So it's natural they won't give a squat about some inherent power to influence the world humans may have, as long as it is too subtle, or too rare. Most just wouldn't care, even if they knew.<br /> <br /> But it could be fun if some Elders,<i> taking in count their long lives and subtle social influence</i>, had chosen to cultivate the inherent occult potential of humanity as a long term project, discovered the Consensus (probably by another name, and with other implications) and started to manipulate it to their advantage.<br /> <br /> For instance: perhaps some of those Elders that like to impersonate a God could be doing so in order to create a worship that benefits them supernaturaly (rather than just for the money and followers). Their abodes are Reality Zones where their word determines what's Vulgar and what's not. Take it up a notch and it could allow them to develop a form of Faith that doesn't hurt them, it could justify keeping some kind of Bygones w/o it being too taxing on blood to sustain, or justify some other forms of Static Magic miracles happening.<br /> <br /> Moreover, while Mages tend to see themselves as shaping human belief to benefit them, if you see things <i>in the really long term</i>, the oppsite it's also true. Mages are shapped by human belief, on the grounds that nearly every Focus/Paradigm comes from human beliefs. Influence the formation of human belief systems, then see how people naturally Awaken to these. Create your own mages. Have your own Tradition even, True Black Hand style, and benefit from Dynamic Magick more directly. If DA mage it's right about the formation of Arete, one could even shape magick itself with belief, influencing the creation of new systems of magick.<br /> <br /> Perhaps &quot;belief&quot; doesn't directly shape anything other than &quot;magic itself&quot;, the magic of humanity - but then, as humanity applies said power, that could be enough to shape the world up to some extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-01-2024, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T08:02:24-07:00","id":1543146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542954#post1542954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also kind of a non-starter, purely academic, argument in the same vein as &quot;what existed before the Big Bang?&quot;. It is, for all intents and purposes, devoid of all practical purpose. The Tapestry exists and so do non-human entities; however, it's human collective consciousness that defines the former, and determines the capability of the latter to interact with and influence the Tapestry.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on what you mean by shaping. I'll agree that the Consensus has an effect on the Tapestry; I've never said otherwise. What I said is that it isn't necessarily the <i>only</i> thing that influences the Tapestry; nor is its influence without limits. <i>Especially</i> in a crossover game. While it may feed a mage's ego to think that vampires and werewolves are manifestations of Magick and subject to the whims of the Consensus, that ain't necessarily so. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542954#post1542954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what's lost in this tangential discussion is Sleepers have Avatars, too. It's through the unconscious influence of sleeping Avatars consensus -- local, regional, or global, historic or contemporary -- forms. That may be the full extent of a sleeping Avatar's influence upon reality and consensus, but that influence still exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking only for myself, I have not lost sight of the fact that Sleepers have Avatars, too; it's an integral part of my view of Mage's metaphysics. But that doesn't mean that Sleeper Avatars define <i>everything</i>. <b>Mage</b> Revised introduced the notion of Cosmological Constants, specifically pointing to the Curse of Caine and <b>Werewolf</b>\u200b's Triat as examples of things that can't just be wished away by the Consensus; and M20 has its Earthly Foundations, which are more broadly aspects of reality that don't change no matter how much the human Consensus says otherwise. Note that that's not a limit on what the Awakened can do; but that's too be expected: a single mage is more powerful than the entire Consensus. If he wasn't, he couldn't work Magick. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1542954#post1542954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are two examples that really present the case, than which we really needn't look further: bygones, and the panoply of cthonic entities that inhabit the Deep Umbra. The plight of bygones speaks for itself, but that the Umbrood inhabiting the Deep Umbra are largely indefinite, indifferent, and by most accounts insapient <i>until impinged upon by human presence</i> speaks to the full extent of human influence on the Tapestry.<br /> <br /> The very fact we can question if these entities even exist in any form other than as Quintessence until observed by Awakened or Sleepers, is in itself the evidence of the point. We can't get around that even the most skeptical and empiricist Awakened mage and their cohort still carries implicit bias and some degree of expectation based on past experience out there, and it's inherently unknowable if, say, the Flying Spaghetti Monster really was out there all along just waiting to be discovered, or if the Flying Spaghetti Monster spontaneously manifested out of Quintessence in response to someone making a dumb quip that made its way through the voidship.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually doesn't say anything useful, any more than the speculation that the moon wouldn't exist if nobody sees it. The fact that the question can be asked tells us nothing, because the question can't be <i>answered</i>. <br /> <br /> On the Bygones, I'll point out that vampires aren't subject to Disbelief. In order to say that the Consensus defines reality, you either need to say that the Consensus accepts the existence of vampires, or that for some unexplained reason, the Consensus' rejection of vampires doesn't manifest the same way as it does for Bygones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T12:06:55-07:00","id":1543155,"title":"","content":"I'd like to add, within WoD vampires, werewolves, fairies and demons don\u2019t just exist, they do so in a manner that isn\u2019t informed by human belief. Their culture, society, powers, strengths and weaknesses, while well known and expected by players, are in many ways counterintuitive to WoD\u2019s humanity.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s also true for many supernatural entities and phenomena they know about. Spirits exist in many shapes and sizes, and no, they\u2019re not all manifestations of human belief. In fact, most of them seem to not give a fuck to what humans believe, including godheads and other spirits that are known by humans in some form.<br /> <br /> Chimeras are particularly interesting: even being born from human minds, they are birthed by imagination, not belief, and would find a creative scientist quite a good company, while a faithful zealot that actually believes in fairies could be too Banal to be around.<br /> <br /> So the Consensus has factual, demonstrable limits on what it can create or destroy about the world. The history of Paradox also isn\u2019t proof of anything: the very fact that Paradox only started to exist at one point in time, and the inconsistency in the forms it took, points more to questions than to answers. Why didn't it exist before? Why did it only affect botches early on? Why it doesn\u2019t affect any other supernatural phenomena other than Awakened Magic? Why did a single, particular battle have so much effect on turning the Scourge into modern Paradox? And if it comes from the Consensus, why are its forms more informed by the beliefs of the very Mage causing it, frequently making things even weirder?<br /> <br /> Even what if scenarios are poor evidence. Be they just thought experiments or umbral realms of their own, they\u2019re another reality to begin with, and as such it is hard to prove their distinctions come from the Consensus being true, or simply from how the Umbra and its realms work. The What If realm may very well correspond to another \u201cconsensus\u201d, but internally that be just due to its own natural laws. Or it may be defined by a Consensual Reality without that really being proof that \u201cbaseline\u201d reality is the same.<br /> <br /> One thing is certain, though: whatever reality exists behind the Consensus, it isn\u2019t necessarily our science being true or anything like that. While it probably contains common sense rules (things fall unless uplift, things don\u2019t change shape and form spontaneously without cause), the details can be as varied as the imagination of the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T13:06:50-07:00","id":1543156,"title":"","content":"And to that, I would add that the Reality Zones section of Mage has two interesting points: the aforementioned Earthly Foundations (which Victorian Mage further indicates is the state that reality gradually returns to if a Reality Zone is fully depopulated), and that the rules for a Reality Zone are defined entirely in terms of howMagick works: what's Vulgar, what's Coincidental, and what sort of difficulty modifier the Magick Effect gets. There's nothing in there about Coincidental Effects becoming nonmagical, or ordinarily nonmagical effects requiring Magick. The binary between what's Magickal and what isn't is fixed. <br /> <br /> So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>' point about &quot;maybe it's just the Awakened&quot; isn't as far fetched as you might think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T18:10:00-07:00","id":1543235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543146#post1543146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends on what you mean by shaping. I'll agree that the Consensus has an effect on the Tapestry; I've never said otherwise. What I said is that it isn't necessarily the <i>only</i> thing that influences the Tapestry; nor is its influence without limits. <i>Especially</i> in a crossover game. While it may feed a mage's ego to think that vampires and werewolves are manifestations of Magick and subject to the whims of the Consensus, that ain't necessarily so...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily disagree; I just believe the argument is purely academic, and doesn't have any implications or practical relevance to the game, its setting, or its metaphysics. As I pointed out, it's like asking what came before the Big Bang: whatever did (if anything), it's unobservable, inherently unknowable and not subject to experimentation or falsification, and at the end of the day our universe already is what it is. To figure out what if anything came before it will -- bare minimum -- require us to have already discovered a &quot;theory of everything&quot;, and at that point anything that <i>might</i> be learned to yield benefit already will have been learned. Ergo, it's largely just a thought experiment...fun perhaps, but in no way practically useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking only for myself, I have not lost sight of the fact that Sleepers have Avatars, too; it's an integral part of my view of Mage's metaphysics... </div> </div> </div>I know you haven't, but others who may or may not be as fluent in MtAs lore/metaphysics as you or I might have. Like you pointed out, it's an integral part of MtAs metaphysics as, in the final analysis, yes it <i>is</i> all &quot;magick&quot; -- intentional or not. Most of it that occurs in the world <i>isn't</i> the result of &quot;willwork&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...<b>Mage</b> Revised introduced the notion of Cosmological Constants, specifically pointing to the Curse of Caine and <b>Werewolf</b>'s Triat as examples of things that can't just be wished away by the Consensus; and M20 has its Earthly Foundations, which are more broadly aspects of reality that don't change no matter how much the human Consensus says otherwise... </div> </div> </div>Those are honestly somewhat silly (even if &quot;RAW&quot;) propositions, when you really consider it. I consider it throwaway fluff to justify crossover content, and little more.<br /> <br /> The Triat and even Triatic Wyrm aren't even inconsistent with MtAs metaphysics...it's the most consistent single point of non-Mage metaphysics there is, to the point Mage metaphysics themselves are dependent on it. For all intents and purposes, the Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm are spiritual manifestations of Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy: it's silly to call that out as an external cosmological constant when it's already an <i>internal</i> cosmological constant.<br /> <br /> And as for vampires -- looping this back to, you know, <i>vampires</i> -- Cainites as such aren't even the only vampires out there. The kuei-jin resemble Risen more than Cainites proper, the Drowned Legacies may not even be Cainites, and while the Laibon are the most straightforward of the bunch the Curse doesn't even manifest in them the same way as other Cainites. In the last case there's hard evidence the Curse of Caine isn't even internally constant, and in the former two there's evidence the Curse of Caine isn't the sole and exclusive point of origin for &quot;vampirism&quot;.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, what <i>is</i> mutable about it are those...let's call them alternative lineages for simplicity...are susceptible and conform to local or regional vampire lore and religious belief. That suggests indeed there is some cross-pollination -- one way or the other, or both -- between Consensus and vampirism.<br /> <br /> That to me doesn't contradict but rather reinforce the quieter both game lines' themes of imperialism, subjugation and oppression, and greed. Over half the world's population follows an Abrahamic religion, and the cultures in which &quot;not necessarily Cainites&quot; found themselves were brutally oppressed, enslaved and/or culturally assimilated, or genocided over the past few centuries...specifically, by those following Abrahamic religions. That's infertile grounds for vampires who <i>aren't</i> Cainites if there's any interdependence between Consensus and vampirism (and there must be), and from that perspective it only makes sense the &quot;last vamps standing&quot; are Cainites and kuei-jin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That actually doesn't say anything useful, any more than the speculation that the moon wouldn't exist if nobody sees it. The fact that the question can be asked tells us nothing, because the question can't be <i>answered</i>. </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much my entire point in a nutshell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the Bygones, I'll point out that vampires aren't subject to Disbelief. In order to say that the Consensus defines reality, you either need to say that the Consensus accepts the existence of vampires, or that for some unexplained reason, the Consensus' rejection of vampires doesn't manifest the same way as it does for Bygones. </div> </div> </div>Unless the &quot;Curse of Caine&quot; is, for one reason or another, itself a manifestation of Disbelief. Disbelief doesn't have to manifest in exactly the same way, every time, for every form of supernatural. As pointed out, for supernaturals that are, or at one point were at least partially human (and therefore possessed of an Avatar), Disbelief <i>doesn't</i> manifest in the form of their poofing out of existence, but rather in a monkey's paw/dramatic irony way. The anthropocentric model still holds for those groups, even if they're no longer fully -- or at all -- human.<br /> <br /> At least in the World of Darkness, there's <i>enough</i> greyspace/soft evidence/god of the gaps -- even fantastical thinking by way of popular culture and science fiction/fantasy -- for those supernaturals to continue existing despite Consensus, but under very restrictive terms as defined by their &quot;curses&quot;. Consensus isn't a binary of &quot;what is&quot; and &quot;what is not&quot;; it's also &quot;what might be&quot;, and as long as a fatsplat like vampires <i>might</i> exist, they <i>can</i> exist.<br /> <br /> In my headcanon, every Cainite as of modern nights has Dracula to thank for their own existence. The unintended, but hilarious, side effect of the Masquerade and its success was that vampires chose to write themselves out of Consensus...until Dracula's little stunt with Bram Stoker, which kept them in the collective consciousness <i>just enough</i> to prevent going Bygones over the 20th Century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T05:03:58-07:00","id":1543259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543235#post1543235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...<b>Mage</b> Revised introduced the notion of Cosmological Constants, specifically pointing to the Curse of Caine and <b>Werewolf</b>'s Triat as examples of things that can't just be wished away by the Consensus; and M20 has its Earthly Foundations, which are more broadly aspects of reality that don't change no matter how much the human Consensus says otherwise... </div> </div> </div>Those are honestly somewhat silly (even if &quot;RAW&quot;) propositions, when you really consider it. I consider it throwaway fluff to justify crossover content, and little more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't consider those points to be at all silly or throwaway fluff; I consider them to be a serious acknowledgment that, again, the Human Consensus isn't the end-all, be-all determiner of the nature of reality. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless the &quot;Curse of Caine&quot; is, for one reason or another, itself a manifestation of Disbelief. </div> </div> </div>But that waters down the term &quot;Disbelief&quot; to the point that it's essentially meaningless. As I said above: &quot;\u2026or that for some unexplained reason, the Consensus' rejection of vampires doesn't manifest the same way as it does for Bygones.&quot; You can always pound the square peg until it eventually fits into the round hole; but if you're not going into this <i>trying </i>to make everything fit into <b>Mage</b>'s metaphysics, a more natural understanding would be that vampires have nothing to do with Magick; they're not sustained by it, and they're not struggling against it. Those are things that are particular to mages; and while other supernaturals exist in the World of Darkness, they exist outside the framework that the Awakened feature.<br /> <br /> And as <i>you</i> said in a slightly difference context:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't necessarily disagree; I just believe the argument is purely academic, and doesn't have any implications or practical relevance to the game, its setting, or its metaphysics. </div> </div> </div>Trying to shoehorn everything into Mage's cosmology and metaphysics has no practical relevance, and serves only the ego of the <b>Mage</b> fan. If you have to spindle and mutilate the term &quot;Disbelief&quot; to the point where it's loose enough that it can apply to <i>any</i> supernatural downsides that anyone faces, then there's no point to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T09:38:32-07:00","id":1543268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543235#post1543235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my headcanon, every Cainite as of modern nights has Dracula to thank for their own existence. The unintended, but hilarious, side effect of the Masquerade and its success was that vampires chose to write themselves out of Consensus...until Dracula's little stunt with Bram Stoker, which kept them in the collective consciousness <i>just enough</i> to prevent going Bygones over the 20th Century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explain why this hasn't happened for Bigfoot, then, given that not only are they constantly in the collective consciousness but 13% of Americans outright believe in them? This also can't explain why sorcerers can do the things that they can do without attracting Paradox while as soon as you Awaken, you cease to be able to do sorcery. If it really was just enough people believing in sorcery to make it possible, emulating sorcery should be coincidental rather than vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T10:42:31-07:00","id":1543271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543268#post1543268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explain why this hasn't happened for Bigfoot, then, given that not only are they constantly in the collective consciousness but 13% of Americans outright believe in them? This also can't explain why sorcerers can do the things that they can do without attracting Paradox while as soon as you Awaken, you cease to be able to do sorcery. If it really was just enough people believing in sorcery to make it possible, emulating sorcery should be coincidental rather than vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, but wasn't there an optional rule where vulgar magic could be used as incidental magic in rural and isolated areas where mysticism persists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T13:55:09-07:00","id":1543281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543271#post1543271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but wasn't there an optional rule where vulgar magic could be used as incidental magic in rural and isolated areas where mysticism persists?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's reality zones. However, sorcery is not affected by reality zones. A Hermetic sorcery can do magic unimpeded in the middle of a Technocratic construct, so long as no one is staring at them while they do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T15:14:15-07:00","id":1543287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543235#post1543235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just believe the argument is purely academic, and doesn't have any implications or practical relevance to the game, its setting, or its metaphysics</div> </div> </div> </div>Being Mage, of all games, this couldn\u2019t be farther from the truth.<br /> <br /> The argument has several implications, because it opens to many different types of stories the group can tell. How the ST chooses to interpret Earthly Foundations and the Consensus tells what can and cannot affect reality and in which way, what are the possible results, and how far from success are the groups involved.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re literally talking about the core of the Ascension War, people \u2018purely academicly\u2019 kill each other because of this.<br /> <br /> For practical uses, determining how much the Consensus is actually shaped by humanity, and how much it shapes reality, is relevant for any game that dares to explore the setting actually evolving from its starting point. It doesn\u2019t even need to be the focus of the game, simply the background being that the status quo somehow changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T15:28:47-07:00","id":1543290,"title":"","content":"Wow I didn't know that Mage The Ascension was such a complex game in comparison to what I know about Mage The Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T17:17:57-07:00","id":1543300,"title":"","content":"Yeah; in terms of philosophy and themes, Mage: the Awakening is Easy Mode compared to Mage: the Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T19:04:26-07:00","id":1543309,"title":"","content":"Nothing wrong about keeping things simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T19:06:42-07:00","id":1543311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543309#post1543309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing wrong about keeping things simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's also why Awakening never quite caught on even like Requiem.<br /> <br /> The Seers of the Throne were probably better bad guys than the Union, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T19:07:39-07:00","id":1543312,"title":"","content":"I liked the Awakening setting, that said the Lost and Requiem were excellent despite lukewarm response from the Masquerade fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-07-2024, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T09:36:58-07:00","id":1543342,"title":"","content":"I'm not dunking on <b>Awakening</b>; I think it's a fabulous game in its own right. And in terms of the crunch, it easily trounces <b>Ascension</b>. But it <i>is</i> narrower in scope, basically assuming that Magic is fundamentally Hermetic in nature, whereas <b>Ascension</b> goes out of its way to make as few assumptions about what Magick is as possible. Which is why there's such a strong temptation to assume that <b>Ascension</b>'s metaphysics encompass <i>everything. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T09:44:20-07:00","id":1543344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543311#post1543311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, it's also why Awakening never quite caught on even like Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to have done just fine, IMHO. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543311#post1543311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Seers of the Throne were probably better bad guys than the Union, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, largely because the Union comes across far more sympathetically than the Seers do: the Seers are better bad guys; but the Technocrats are by far the more nuanced and interesting. <br /> <br /> But at this point, we're getting pretty far afield. This is, after all, a Masquerade thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T10:04:52-07:00","id":1543347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543344#post1543344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, largely because the Union comes across far more sympathetically than the Seers do: the Seers are better bad guys; but the Technocrats are by far the more nuanced and interesting.<br /> <br /> But at this point, we're getting pretty far afield. This is, after all, a Masquerade thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is kind of the problem.<br /> <br /> You have the anti-democratic genocidal Illuminati as the progressive rationalists in Mage. Basically, putting them as....fascists.<br /> <br /> It's kind of sick when you think about it.<br /> <br /> Because even at their most sympathetic, the Technocracy treat humanity as having no say in its own destiny and have a plan to exterminate all supernaturals and their kinfolk as well as suppress all beliefs but their own.<br /> <br /> It's like playing Warhammer 40K really and embracing the theocratic genocidal ethos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T10:42:06-07:00","id":1543349,"title":"","content":"To be fair, that's part and parcel of <b>Mage</b>: even the <i>Traditions</i> have a tendency to decide that they know what's good for you better than you do. It's part of the theme of hubris that's so core to the game. The mage that's truly humble and willing to work alongside humanity instead of trying to tell them what to do is kind of like the vampire who has achieves Golconda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T15:37:14-07:00","id":1543364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543347#post1543347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is kind of the problem.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> It's like playing Warhammer 40K really and embracing the theocratic genocidal ethos.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a problem, it's how Ascension works at its best. And nowadays we have Threat Null to make EVIL Techies.<br /> <br /> Also, embracing the theocratic genocidal ethos is the whole point of playing 40K.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T15:50:12-07:00","id":1543366,"title":"","content":"To be fair Warhammer 40K is meant as a Grimdark future where everyone is warring with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T19:20:48-07:00","id":1543377,"title":"","content":"It reminds me of Shadowrun to an extent. Original recipe Mage made it clear that the Traditions may have their differences but everyone knew they were doing the same sort of magic with different flavors. The Technocracy were fascists and why the Earth was the shithole it was with the rich and powerful crushing the poor. Gradually, the Technocrats became more and more reformed while they kept arguing the Traditions were just one bad day of turning on each other (and would absolutely start slaughtering each other once the Technocrats were gone).<br /> <br /> In Shadowrun, it basically had a similar trajectory. The first editions are all about being a bunch of Robin Hoods and angry punks striking at the Man and often using the man's nunyen to do it. It's about living free and dying hard. Later editions (4th and 5th) then took a turn to the grimdark where the Shadowrunners were a bunch of cold blooded sociopaths who scorned the idea of doing anything but wetwork for the corporations.<br /> <br /> Vampire has its own trajectory to get us back on the original subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T20:41:17-07:00","id":1543389,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say that the Shadowrunners were sociopaths, but then I always played them as pragmatic hired guns who knew that they were criminals and had ethical qualms about doing certain jobs. But we're going off topic and this topic is about not making Kindred uncool. So what are some notions on bringing back the it factors to this setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T15:53:56-07:00","id":1543456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543377#post1543377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Original recipe Mage made it clear that the Traditions may have their differences but everyone knew they were doing the same sort of magic with different flavors. The Technocracy were fascists and why the Earth was the shithole it was with the rich and powerful crushing the poor. Gradually, the Technocrats became more and more reformed while they kept arguing the Traditions were just one bad day of turning on each other (and would absolutely start slaughtering each other once the Technocrats were gone).</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, becoming more complex and nuanced with time is par of the course. As time goes on, players and developers explore new perspectives, expand content, create a history for the setting, and things just can\u2019t remain so simple.<br /> <br /> But above that, 1st edition Mage simply has too many problems. It is a luddite game where new technology and science are only good when done \u201cartistically\u201d, where personal freedom is the only right way to do things, where the modern world is objectively bad in every regard and we should collectively get back to the \u201cbetter days\u201d of an extremely romanticized Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> This is patently untrue, and dangerously so. Life is far more complicated, and ideologies are dangerous when you lose sight of real life nuances. Just to keep it at the most basic example, 1st ed Mage is anti-vax and anti-scientific in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T15:58:30-07:00","id":1543457,"title":"","content":"Nuances are needed as real life is not so simple and people and organizations are not just one thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T18:30:38-07:00","id":1543472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543389#post1543389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say that the Shadowrunners were sociopaths, but then I always played them as pragmatic hired guns who knew that they were criminals and had ethical qualms about doing certain jobs. But we're going off topic and this topic is about not making Kindred uncool. So what are some notions on bringing back the it factors to this setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>My runner groups somehow always ended up running community groups and no cost clinics and legal aid.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T20:04:24-07:00","id":1543484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543456#post1543456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First of all, becoming more complex and nuanced with time is par of the course. As time goes on, players and developers explore new perspectives, expand content, create a history for the setting, and things just can\u2019t remain so simple.<br /> <br /> But above that, 1st edition Mage simply has too many problems. It is a luddite game where new technology and science are only good when done \u201cartistically\u201d, where personal freedom is the only right way to do things, where the modern world is objectively bad in every regard and we should collectively get back to the \u201cbetter days\u201d of an extremely romanticized Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> This is patently untrue, and dangerously so. Life is far more complicated, and ideologies are dangerous when you lose sight of real life nuances. Just to keep it at the most basic example, 1st ed Mage is anti-vax and anti-scientific in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm from the Deep South and my opinion on Technocracy nuance is summarized this way, &quot;As a child, I learned that the Civil War was fought over slavery. As a teenager, I was told it was much more nuanced than that involving many factors. As an adult, I figured out those were all smoke screens for being about slavery.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is to say that it doesn't matter what the Technocracy claims they're about, they're fascists so have to go.<br /> <br /> All of them.<br /> <br /> You can't talk around, &quot;We are engaged in a murder of everyone who disagrees with us as well as the genocide of every supernatural because it doesn't fit our view of humanity.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Post