er that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T20:52:33-07:00","id":1543487,"title":"","content":"I know what you mean about reading about the Civil War and how it wasn't just any one thing and people on both sides thought they were in the right. To this day there is scores of books written about it and documentaries such as one the PBS did some years back.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T22:17:03-07:00","id":1543493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1539041#post1539041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty tired of people hitting the &quot;banes in household products and fast food!&quot; button, though. That was 1e; it got retconned out after for putting something akin to the presence of kegare in everything to throw the Garou off the scent instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that wasn't retcon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T23:33:18-07:00","id":1543496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CamaradaDoppio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543493#post1543493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that wasn't retcon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. From 2e on, taint is widespread and can attract banes but the banes have to come from somewhere else. Subsidiaries even made a specific note that if you did try it, you would tank your business because being around a bane feels awful and Sunburst Computers got chewed up for exactly that reason. So, no more &quot;banes in every product&quot;. Just the essence of uncleanliness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T23:54:54-07:00","id":1543498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543484#post1543484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm from the Deep South and my opinion on Technocracy nuance is summarized this way, &quot;As a child, I learned that the Civil War was fought over slavery. As a teenager, I was told it was much more nuanced than that involving many factors. As an adult, I figured out those were all smoke screens for being about slavery.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is to say that it doesn't matter what the Technocracy claims they're about, they're fascists so have to go.<br /> <br /> All of them.<br /> <br /> You can't talk around, &quot;We are engaged in a murder of everyone who disagrees with us as well as the genocide of every supernatural because it doesn't fit our view of humanity.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm disabled and immunocompromised as a result, amongst other things. As offended as you can note you are by the portrayal of the Technocracy and compare it to Civil War apologia, anti vaxx and anti science sentiment nearly killed me during Covid as far as members of my own family that bought into that, and may just yet someday. Since we never actually left Covid, we've just decided to as a society pretend it's no longer a serious threat and violently attack the idea of maybe masking so the disabled community can do things like travel to their medical treatments without rolling the dice with their lives. Mage 1e basically being an outright celebration of anti medical sentiment, the early WoD's in general baffling hatred of science and scientists (which even made it into Exalted of all things with that whole &quot;do not trust the lies the scientists told you&quot; nonsense promos) to the point of only valorizing things like Etherite junk science makes me livid beyond ways I have to express. You can't talk around &quot;it's not anti vaxx conspiracy bullcrap if the game says this time it's actually true and also faith healing could totally heal you anyway in Mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> Expansion: I have pretty severe Crohn's disease, amongst other things. Indoor plumbing and advanced sanitation are pretty crucial to my life being something vaguely north of some really gross horror. Mage's romantic valorizing of the medieval era and lifestyles as something to long for as related is some deeply ableist stuff while I'm there.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well in Mage all the beliefs that would make your life a living hell and or straight up kill you wouldn't, because of how magically correct they are, and how much of a lie the things keeping you alive are instead&quot; is not the defense of Mage people seem to think it is when I note my offense at all this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  punctuation 10-10-2024, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T02:05:33-07:00","id":1543503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543484#post1543484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm from the Deep South and my opinion on Technocracy nuance is summarized this way, &quot;As a child, I learned that the Civil War was fought over slavery. As a teenager, I was told it was much more nuanced than that involving many factors. As an adult, I figured out those were all smoke screens for being about slavery.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is to say that it doesn't matter what the Technocracy claims they're about, they're fascists so have to go.<br /> <br /> All of them.<br /> <br /> You can't talk around, &quot;We are engaged in a murder of everyone who disagrees with us as well as the genocide of every supernatural because it doesn't fit our view of humanity.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s an interesting example of how much you\u2019re missing the point, you know why?<br /> <br /> In Mage 1st ed, the Traditions have slaves and this is good.<br /> <br /> Consors are basically slaves in their traditional form. They follow Plato\u2019s notion of Philosopher Kings, in which as morally and intellectually superior beings, Mages have a right to govern their inferiors, and everyone is somehow better for this. While the Union has mindless employees.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re missing the point completely because you\u2019re obsessed on your view that the Designated Fascists of the game have to be completely wrong since they\u2019re Fascist, and missing that the whole designation is arbitrary and the Designated Heroes may inadvertently been exposing fascist views.<br /> <br /> Which is exactly what was happening in Mage 1st.<br /> <br /> Mage didn\u2019t change its presentation of the groups to say that fascists sometimes are good. It did so to explore how neither group was actually a good representation of fascism, and to say that a good Mage risks becoming or supporting a fascist without noticing if they follow blindly.<br /> <br /> Crafts are another good example of this. Are they representatives of oppressed communities? Yes, they are. But they\u2019re also frequently hardline traditionalists that protect old structures of internal oppression and supremacist ideologies. It may be easy to miss that when you only look at imperialism from the POV of someone living in the imperialist country, but look at people like Nerandra Modi, Benjamin Netanyahu and Jair Bolsonaro, and you\u2019ll see that they\u2019re always either members or very close to groups that would be Crafts in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T03:43:45-07:00","id":1543510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538996-v-tm-walk-among-us-or-how-5th-edition-makes-vampires-uncool?p=1543503#post1543503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s an interesting example of how much you\u2019re missing the point, you know why?<br /> <br /> In Mage 1st ed, the Traditions have slaves and this is good.<br /> <br /> Consors are basically slaves in their traditional form. They follow Plato\u2019s notion of Philosopher Kings, in which as morally and intellectually superior beings, Mages have a right to govern their inferiors, and everyone is somehow better for this. While the Union has mindless employees.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re missing the point completely because you\u2019re obsessed on your view that the Designated Fascists of the game have to be completely wrong since they\u2019re Fascist, and missing that the whole designation is arbitrary and the Designated Heroes may inadvertently been exposing fascist views.<br /> <br /> Which is exactly what was happening in Mage 1st.<br /> <br /> Mage didn\u2019t change its presentation of the groups to say that fascists sometimes are good. It did so to explore how neither group was actually a good representation of fascism, and to say that a good Mage risks becoming or supporting a fascist without noticing if they follow blindly.<br /> <br /> Crafts are another good example of this. Are they representatives of oppressed communities? Yes, they are. But they\u2019re also frequently hardline traditionalists that protect old structures of internal oppression and supremacist ideologies. It may be easy to miss that when you only look at imperialism from the POV of someone living in the imperialist country, but look at people like Nerandra Modi, Benjamin Netanyahu and Jair Bolsonaro, and you\u2019ll see that they\u2019re always either members or very close to groups that would be Crafts in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I take a lot back because it occurs to me that I'm falling into a trap.<br /> <br /> Which that mage has ever been CONSISTENT about its portrayals.<br /> <br /> A lot of times the versions shown are wholly and deliberately contradictory.<br /> <br /> And it's not a new angle to look at them so much as wholesale retcons.<br /> <br /> Basically, the reverse of the Get of Fenris.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Get of Fenris have been anti-Nazi, anti-racist, largely composed of the people the Nazi killed, and killed all of its racist members for three editions then suddenly all of them became Nazis.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Union of first edition is not the Union of Revised or 20th.<br /> <br /> My apologies.<br /> <br /> The Traditions and Union are whatever the ST says they are at a table and you can find support for whatever interpretation you're going for.<br /> <br /> I just like a mage of oppressed people against the System that tries to kill me and my friends.<br /> <br /> I forgot that is just one style and who &quot;The System&quot; is can vary tremendously. In Excalibur by Tini Howard, the Far Right racist group controlling Britain is a bunch of Verbena-esque witches because some real life upper class neo-paganism groups is FULL of racist assholes.<br /> <br /> Please accept an apology Laser Cannon and Steam-powered Spaceship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cth